ern. 일어나다 (to happen) → 일어나지 않아요 (does not happen).", "ex_ko": "하지만 같은 지역에서 사는 경우는 많지 않아요.", "ex_en": "However, cases where they live in the same area are not common."}, {"name": "~은/는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Topic particle marking the subject. 보호구역은 (the reserve).", "ex_ko": "사리스카 호랑이 보호구역은 인도에서 유명한 곳이에요.", "ex_en": "The Sariska tiger reserve is a famous place in India."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Progressive aspect indicating ongoing action. 살다 (to live) → 살고 있어요 (are living).", "ex_ko": "많은 야생 동물들이 살고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Many wild animals live there."}, {"name": "~기 위해", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Purpose connector. ~기 (nominalizer) + 위해 (for the sake of). Indicates the purpose of an action.", "ex_ko": "호랑이를 보호하기 위해 만든 특별한 공원이에요.", "ex_en": "It is a special park made to protect tigers."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 만들다 drops ㄹ: 만들다 → 만든 공원 (a park that was made).", "ex_ko": "호랑이를 보호하기 위해 만든 특별한 공원이에요.", "ex_en": "It is a special park made to protect tigers."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Possessive particle. 동물들의 (of the animals) indicates ownership/relationship.", "ex_ko": "야생에서 동물들의 생활을 보여주는 흥미로운 사건이에요.", "ex_en": "It is an interesting event showing the life of animals in the wild."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility: ''can''. 느끼다 (to feel) → 느낄 수 있어요 (can feel).", "ex_ko": "자연의 힘을 느낄 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "We can feel the power of nature."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mon2k905xv77' and md5(translation) = '91c3ac65774a6eb0a5d0901fdeae158b';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Boston City in the United States removed a highway that passed through the city center and created a long park called a Greenway. This park runs through the center of the city and provides a resting space for citizens.", "Boston City chose to move the highway underground. They relocated the highway that was on the ground to beneath the earth, clearing the space above.", "In Korea, there are also cases like Seoul''s Cheonggyecheon where roads or elevated highways were removed and parks were created. These projects have the effect of improving the urban environment and enhancing the quality of life for citizens.", "It is a good example showing the trend of urban development changing from a car-centered to a people-centered approach. Many cities are attempting this kind of change."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국 보스턴시가 도심을 지나던 고속도로를 없애고 그린웨이(Greenway)라는 긴 공원을 만들었어요.", "translation": "The city of Boston in the United States removed the highway that ran through downtown and built a long park called the Greenway.", "vocab": [{"ko": "도심", "en": "downtown; urban center"}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass through"}, {"ko": "없애다", "en": "to remove; to eliminate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~던", "exp": "Describes a noun with an action that used to happen in the past. 지나다 → 지나던 고속도로 (the highway that used to pass through).", "example_in_sentence": "지나던 고속도로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending that joins two consecutive or related actions; 없애다 → 없애고 (remove AND create).", "example_in_sentence": "없애고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는", "exp": "Attributive connector meaning ''called; named''; links a name/label to the noun it modifies.", "example_in_sentence": "그린웨이(Greenway)라는 긴 공원"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending; 만들다 → 만들었어요 (created).", "example_in_sentence": "만들었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 공원은 도시 중심부를 가로지르며 시민들에게 휴식 공간을 제공하고 있어요.", "translation": "This park runs across the city center and gives citizens a place to relax.", "vocab": [{"ko": "중심부", "en": "center; central area"}, {"ko": "가로지르다", "en": "to run across; to traverse"}, {"ko": "휴식", "en": "rest; relaxation"}, {"ko": "제공하다", "en": "to provide"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)며", "exp": "Joins two actions or facts: ''while; and''. 가로지르다 → 가로지르며 (runs across and ...).", "example_in_sentence": "가로지르며"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive/continuous aspect marker in polite form; indicates an ongoing action.", "example_in_sentence": "제공하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "보스턴시는 고속도로를 지하로 옮기는 방법을 선택했어요.", "translation": "Boston chose the method of moving the highway underground.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지하", "en": "underground; below ground"}, {"ko": "옮기다", "en": "to move; to relocate"}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method; way"}, {"ko": "선택하다", "en": "to choose; to select"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Attributive ending for present/general actions; 옮기다 → 옮기는 (the method of moving).", "example_in_sentence": "옮기는 방법"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending; 선택하다 → 선택했어요 (chose).", "example_in_sentence": "선택했어요"}]}, {"text": "지상에 있던 고속도로를 땅속으로 옮겨서 위쪽 공간을 비워낸 거예요.", "translation": "They moved the highway that was above ground underground and cleared the upper space.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지상", "en": "above ground; ground level"}, {"ko": "땅속", "en": "underground; below ground"}, {"ko": "비워내다", "en": "to clear out; to empty out"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~던", "exp": "Describes a noun by a past state that has ended. 있다 → 있던 고속도로 (the highway that used to be there).", "example_in_sentence": "있던 고속도로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "Links an action to the next one done by means of it. 옮기다 → 옮겨서 (by moving it, ...).", "example_in_sentence": "옮겨서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 거예요", "exp": "Explains what happened: ''what they did was ...''. 비워내다 → 비워낸 거예요 (they cleared it out).", "example_in_sentence": "비워낸 거예요"}]}, {"text": "한국에서도 서울의 청계천처럼 도로나 고가도로를 없애고 공원을 만든 사례가 있어요.", "translation": "Korea also has cases, like Seoul''s Cheonggyecheon, where roads or overpasses were removed and parks were built.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고가도로", "en": "elevated highway; overpass"}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "case; example; instance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~처럼", "exp": "Postposition meaning ''like; similar to; in the manner of''; indicates a comparison or analogy.", "example_in_sentence": "청계천처럼"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~나", "exp": "Coordinating postposition joining alternatives; 도로나 고가도로 (roads or elevated highways).", "example_in_sentence": "도로나 고가도로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending joining sequential actions; 없애고 (remove and create).", "example_in_sentence": "없애고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 만들다 drops ㄹ: 만들다 → 만든 사례 (cases where parks were made).", "example_in_sentence": "만든 사례"}]}, {"text": "이런 사업들은 도시 환경을 개선하고 시민들의 삶의 질을 높이는 효과가 있어요.", "translation": "These projects have the effect of improving urban environment and raising citizens'' quality of life.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사업", "en": "project; business; undertaking"}, {"ko": "환경", "en": "environment"}, {"ko": "개선하다", "en": "to improve"}, {"ko": "높이다", "en": "to raise; to increase"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending joining two effects; 개선하다 → 개선하고 (improve and raise).", "example_in_sentence": "개선하고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Attributive ending for actions that produce effects; 높이다 → 높이는 (the effect of raising).", "example_in_sentence": "높이는 효과"}]}, {"text": "도시 개발에서 자동차 중심에서 사람 중심으로 바뀌는 추세를 보여주는 좋은 사례예요.", "translation": "It is a good example showing a trend of shifting from car-centered to people-centered urban development.", "vocab": [{"ko": "중심", "en": "center; focus; priority"}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change; to shift"}, {"ko": "추세", "en": "trend"}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to demonstrate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에서 ~(으)로", "exp": "Postposition pair expressing change/transition from one state to another; from car-centered to people-centered.", "example_in_sentence": "자동차 중심에서 사람 중심으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Attributive ending for ongoing/general actions; 바뀌다 → 바뀌는 (the trend of shifting).", "example_in_sentence": "바뀌는 추세"}]}, {"text": "많은 도시들이 이런 변화를 시도하고 있어요.", "translation": "Many cities are attempting this kind of change.", "vocab": [{"ko": "변화", "en": "change; transformation"}, {"ko": "시도하다", "en": "to attempt; to try"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive/continuous aspect in polite form; indicates an ongoing attempt.", "example_in_sentence": "시도하고 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "도심", "en": "downtown; urban center", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass through", "note": ""}, {"ko": "없애다", "en": "to remove; to eliminate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중심부", "en": "center; central area", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가로지르다", "en": "to run across; to traverse", "note": ""}, {"ko": "휴식", "en": "rest; relaxation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제공하다", "en": "to provide", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지하", "en": "underground; below ground", "note": ""}, {"ko": "옮기다", "en": "to move; to relocate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method; way", "note": ""}, {"ko": "선택하다", "en": "to choose; to select", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지상", "en": "above ground; ground level", "note": ""}, {"ko": "땅속", "en": "underground; below ground", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비워내다", "en": "to clear out; to empty out", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고가도로", "en": "elevated highway; overpass", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "case; example; instance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사업", "en": "project; business; undertaking", "note": ""}, {"ko": "환경", "en": "environment", "note": ""}, {"ko": "개선하다", "en": "to improve", "note": ""}, {"ko": "높이다", "en": "to raise; to increase", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중심", "en": "center; focus; priority", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change; to shift", "note": ""}, {"ko": "추세", "en": "trend", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to demonstrate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "변화", "en": "change; transformation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시도하다", "en": "to attempt; to try", "note": ""}, {"word": "고속도로", "reading": "gogsokdoro", "meaning": "highway; expressway", "context": "도심을 지나던 고속도로를 없애고"}, {"word": "공원", "reading": "gongwon", "meaning": "park", "context": "긴 공원을 만들었어요"}, {"word": "그린웨이", "reading": "geurinwe", "meaning": "greenway (a long park or recreational corridor)", "context": "그린웨이(Greenway)라는 긴 공원을"}, {"word": "삶의 질", "reading": "salmui jil", "meaning": "quality of life", "context": "시민들의 삶의 질을 높이는"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~던", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes a noun with an action that used to happen in the past. 지나다 → 지나던 고속도로 (the highway that used to pass through).", "ex_ko": "미국 보스턴시가 도심을 지나던 고속도로를 없애고 그린웨이(Greenway)라는 긴 공원을 만들었어요.", "ex_en": "The city of Boston in the United States removed the highway that ran through downtown and built a long park called the Greenway."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connective ending that joins two consecutive or related actions; 없애다 → 없애고 (remove AND create).", "ex_ko": "미국 보스턴시가 도심을 지나던 고속도로를 없애고 그린웨이(Greenway)라는 긴 공원을 만들었어요.", "ex_en": "The city of Boston in the United States removed the highway that ran through downtown and built a long park called the Greenway."}, {"name": "~(이)라는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Attributive connector meaning ''called; named''; links a name/label to the noun it modifies.", "ex_ko": "미국 보스턴시가 도심을 지나던 고속도로를 없애고 그린웨이(Greenway)라는 긴 공원을 만들었어요.", "ex_en": "The city of Boston in the United States removed the highway that ran through downtown and built a long park called the Greenway."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense polite ending; 만들다 → 만들었어요 (created).", "ex_ko": "미국 보스턴시가 도심을 지나던 고속도로를 없애고 그린웨이(Greenway)라는 긴 공원을 만들었어요.", "ex_en": "The city of Boston in the United States removed the highway that ran through downtown and built a long park called the Greenway."}, {"name": "~(으)며", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Joins two actions or facts: ''while; and''. 가로지르다 → 가로지르며 (runs across and ...).", "ex_ko": "이 공원은 도시 중심부를 가로지르며 시민들에게 휴식 공간을 제공하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "This park runs across the city center and gives citizens a place to relax."}, {"name": "~고 있어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive/continuous aspect marker in polite form; indicates an ongoing action.", "ex_ko": "이 공원은 도시 중심부를 가로지르며 시민들에게 휴식 공간을 제공하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "This park runs across the city center and gives citizens a place to relax."}, {"name": "~는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Attributive ending for actions that produce effects; 높이다 → 높이는 (the effect of raising).", "ex_ko": "보스턴시는 고속도로를 지하로 옮기는 방법을 선택했어요.", "ex_en": "Boston chose the method of moving the highway underground."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Links an action to the next one done by means of it. 옮기다 → 옮겨서 (by moving it, ...).", "ex_ko": "지상에 있던 고속도로를 땅속으로 옮겨서 위쪽 공간을 비워낸 거예요.", "ex_en": "They moved the highway that was above ground underground and cleared the upper space."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 거예요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Explains what happened: ''what they did was ...''. 비워내다 → 비워낸 거예요 (they cleared it out).", "ex_ko": "지상에 있던 고속도로를 땅속으로 옮겨서 위쪽 공간을 비워낸 거예요.", "ex_en": "They moved the highway that was above ground underground and cleared the upper space."}, {"name": "~나", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Coordinating postposition joining alternatives; 도로나 고가도로 (roads or elevated highways).", "ex_ko": "한국에서도 서울의 청계천처럼 도로나 고가도로를 없애고 공원을 만든 사례가 있어요.", "ex_en": "Korea also has cases, like Seoul''s Cheonggyecheon, where roads or overpasses were removed and parks were built."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 만들다 drops ㄹ: 만들다 → 만든 사례 (cases where parks were made).", "ex_ko": "한국에서도 서울의 청계천처럼 도로나 고가도로를 없애고 공원을 만든 사례가 있어요.", "ex_en": "Korea also has cases, like Seoul''s Cheonggyecheon, where roads or overpasses were removed and parks were built."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mon2kwagcup6' and md5(translation) = '4d9cdde9d00d91bfecc1e74e972974ed';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There is a fascinating place in an American desert. That place is called Racetrack Playa. Here, large rocks move by themselves.", "Scientists were curious for a long time. They didn''t know why rocks moved by themselves. Rocks move on their own without anyone pushing them.", "Recently, they found out the reason. In winter, when it rains, thin ice forms. And when the wind blows, the ice pushes the rocks.", "When the ice melts, only the rocks remain. That''s why the rocks appear to move by themselves. It''s a truly fascinating natural phenomenon."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국 사막에 신기한 곳이 있어요.", "translation": "There is a mysterious place in the American desert.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사막", "en": "desert"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be fascinating"}, {"ko": "곳", "en": "place"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요", "exp": "Present tense ending for declarative statements. Polite, informal style.", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}, {"text": "그곳 이름은 레이스트랙 플라야예요.", "translation": "That place''s name is Racetrack Playa.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이름", "en": "name"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요/이에요", "exp": "Polite form of 이다 (to be). After a vowel use 예요: 플라야 → 플라야예요 (is Playa).", "example_in_sentence": "플라야예요"}]}, {"text": "여기서는 큰 바위들이 혼자서 움직여요.", "translation": "Here, large rocks move by themselves.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바위", "en": "rock"}, {"ko": "혼자", "en": "alone; by oneself"}, {"ko": "움직이다", "en": "to move"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (topic particle)", "exp": "The topic marker 는 added to 여기서 (here) sets the scene: ''here, (in this place)''.", "example_in_sentence": "여기서는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요", "exp": "Present tense ending.", "example_in_sentence": "움직여요"}]}, {"text": "과학자들이 오랫동안 궁금해했어요.", "translation": "Scientists were curious for a long time.", "vocab": [{"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist"}, {"ko": "오랫동안", "en": "for a long time"}, {"ko": "궁금해하다", "en": "to wonder; to be curious"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어하다", "exp": "Turns a feeling adjective into a verb about someone''s feeling. 궁금하다 (curious) → 궁금해하다 (to wonder) → 궁금해했어요 (wondered).", "example_in_sentence": "궁금해했어요"}]}, {"text": "바위가 왜 혼자 움직이는지 몰랐거든요.", "translation": "Because they didn''t know why rocks moved by themselves.", "vocab": [{"ko": "왜", "en": "why"}, {"ko": "모르다", "en": "to not know"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는지", "exp": "Embedded question marker. Connects question clause to main verb.", "example_in_sentence": "움직이는지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었- (past)", "exp": "Past tense. 모르다 is 르-irregular: 모르다 → 몰랐- (didn''t know).", "example_in_sentence": "몰랐"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~거든요", "exp": "Gives the reason for what was just said: ''you see, (it''s because) ...''.", "example_in_sentence": "몰랐거든요"}]}, {"text": "사람이 밀지도 않는데 바위가 저절로 이동해요.", "translation": "Even though no one pushes, rocks move by themselves.", "vocab": [{"ko": "밀다", "en": "to push"}, {"ko": "저절로", "en": "by itself; automatically"}, {"ko": "이동하다", "en": "to move; to relocate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지도 않다", "exp": "Negation with added emphasis (neither/not even). 밀다 → 밀지도 않는다.", "example_in_sentence": "밀지도 않는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는데", "exp": "Concessive connective. Contrasts with next clause.", "example_in_sentence": "않는데"}]}, {"text": "최근에 그 이유를 알아냈어요.", "translation": "Recently, they found out the reason.", "vocab": [{"ko": "최근", "en": "recently"}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason"}, {"ko": "알아내다", "en": "to find out"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 알아내다 (to find out) → 알아냈어요 (found out).", "example_in_sentence": "알아냈어요"}]}, {"text": "겨울에 비가 오면 얇은 얼음이 생겨요.", "translation": "When it rains in winter, thin ice forms.", "vocab": [{"ko": "겨울", "en": "winter"}, {"ko": "비", "en": "rain"}, {"ko": "얇다", "en": "to be thin"}, {"ko": "얼음", "en": "ice"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~면", "exp": "Conditional connector. If/when condition is met.", "example_in_sentence": "오면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요", "exp": "Present tense. 생기다 → 생겨요.", "example_in_sentence": "생겨요"}]}, {"text": "그리고 바람이 불면 얼음이 바위를 밀어요.", "translation": "And when wind blows, ice pushes rocks.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바람", "en": "wind"}, {"ko": "불다", "en": "to blow"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~면", "exp": "Conditional marker. If/when.", "example_in_sentence": "불면"}]}, {"text": "얼음이 녹으면 바위만 남아 있어요.", "translation": "When ice melts, only rocks remain.", "vocab": [{"ko": "녹다", "en": "to melt"}, {"ko": "남다", "en": "to remain"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~면", "exp": "Conditional marker.", "example_in_sentence": "녹으면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~만", "exp": "Exclusive particle. Only.", "example_in_sentence": "바위만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다", "exp": "Continuous state. 남다 → 남아 있어요 = remains in a state.", "example_in_sentence": "남아 있어요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 바위가 혼자 움직인 것처럼 보여요.", "translation": "That''s why rocks appear to have moved by themselves.", "vocab": [], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것처럼", "exp": "Means ''as if something happened''. 움직이다 → 움직인 것처럼 (as if they had moved).", "example_in_sentence": "움직인 것처럼"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요", "exp": "Present tense. 보이다 → 보여요.", "example_in_sentence": "보여요"}]}, {"text": "정말 신기한 자연 현상이에요.", "translation": "It''s truly a fascinating natural phenomenon.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정말", "en": "really; truly"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be fascinating"}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature"}, {"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요", "exp": "Polite form of 이다 (to be) after a consonant. 현상 → 현상이에요 (is a phenomenon).", "example_in_sentence": "현상이에요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "사막", "en": "desert", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be fascinating", "note": ""}, {"ko":