ve by themselves."}, {"name": "~아/어하다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Turns a feeling adjective into a verb about someone''s feeling. 궁금하다 (curious) → 궁금해하다 (to wonder) → 궁금해했어요 (wondered).", "ex_ko": "과학자들이 오랫동안 궁금해했어요.", "ex_en": "Scientists were curious for a long time."}, {"name": "~는지", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Embedded question marker. Connects question clause to main verb.", "ex_ko": "바위가 왜 혼자 움직이는지 몰랐거든요.", "ex_en": "Because they didn''t know why rocks moved by themselves."}, {"name": "~았/었- (past)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past tense. 모르다 is 르-irregular: 모르다 → 몰랐- (didn''t know).", "ex_ko": "바위가 왜 혼자 움직이는지 몰랐거든요.", "ex_en": "Because they didn''t know why rocks moved by themselves."}, {"name": "~거든요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Gives the reason for what was just said: ''you see, (it''s because) ...''.", "ex_ko": "바위가 왜 혼자 움직이는지 몰랐거든요.", "ex_en": "Because they didn''t know why rocks moved by themselves."}, {"name": "~지도 않다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Negation with added emphasis (neither/not even). 밀다 → 밀지도 않는다.", "ex_ko": "사람이 밀지도 않는데 바위가 저절로 이동해요.", "ex_en": "Even though no one pushes, rocks move by themselves."}, {"name": "~는데", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Concessive connective. Contrasts with next clause.", "ex_ko": "사람이 밀지도 않는데 바위가 저절로 이동해요.", "ex_en": "Even though no one pushes, rocks move by themselves."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past tense. 알아내다 (to find out) → 알아냈어요 (found out).", "ex_ko": "최근에 그 이유를 알아냈어요.", "ex_en": "Recently, they found out the reason."}, {"name": "~면", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Conditional connector. If/when condition is met.", "ex_ko": "겨울에 비가 오면 얇은 얼음이 생겨요.", "ex_en": "When it rains in winter, thin ice forms."}, {"name": "~만", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Exclusive particle. Only.", "ex_ko": "얼음이 녹으면 바위만 남아 있어요.", "ex_en": "When ice melts, only rocks remain."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Continuous state. 남다 → 남아 있어요 = remains in a state.", "ex_ko": "얼음이 녹으면 바위만 남아 있어요.", "ex_en": "When ice melts, only rocks remain."}, {"name": "~이에요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Polite form of 이다 (to be) after a consonant. 현상 → 현상이에요 (is a phenomenon).", "ex_ko": "정말 신기한 자연 현상이에요.", "ex_en": "It''s truly a fascinating natural phenomenon."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mon2lpefs7nl' and md5(translation) = 'bec8451e9cd4751f13c5719ea7746251';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Someone created a special geometric shape out of snow. This shape is a polygon with multiple faces.", "More and more people are creating snow sculptures. It''s a fun activity that can be enjoyed during the cold winter.", "People who saw this artwork were very surprised. It''s amazing that such a detailed shape can be made from snow.", "In our country, people also make snowmen every winter. However, creating such complex geometric shapes is not easy."], "sentences": [{"text": "누군가가 눈으로 특별한 도형을 만들었어요.", "translation": "Someone made a special shape out of snow.", "vocab": [{"ko": "누군가", "en": "someone"}, {"ko": "눈", "en": "snow"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "도형", "en": "shape"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~으로 (instrumental particle)", "exp": "Marks the material or means used to make/create something. 눈 (snow) → 눈으로 (with/out of snow).", "example_in_sentence": "눈으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks completion of past action in polite/casual style. 만들다 → 만들었어요 (made).", "example_in_sentence": "만들었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 도형은 여러 개의 면이 있는 다각형(polygon)이에요.", "translation": "This shape is a polygon with multiple sides.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이", "en": "this"}, {"ko": "여러", "en": "several; many"}, {"ko": "면", "en": "side; face"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to have"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present participle / attributive ending)", "exp": "Modifies the noun 다각형 to describe its property. 있다 → 있는 (that has/with).", "example_in_sentence": "있는 다각형"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "이에요 (copula, polite present)", "exp": "Copular verb in polite style. Links subject to predicate noun. 다각형 + 이에요 (is a polygon).", "example_in_sentence": "다각형(polygon)이에요"}]}, {"text": "눈조각상을 만드는 사람들이 점점 늘고 있어요.", "translation": "The number of people making snow sculptures is gradually increasing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "눈조각상", "en": "snow sculpture"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person"}, {"ko": "점점", "en": "gradually"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present participle / attributive ending)", "exp": "Modifies 사람들 to indicate the continuous action. 만들다 → 만드는 (that make/making).", "example_in_sentence": "만드는 사람들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (progressive aspect)", "exp": "Expresses ongoing or continuous action/state. 늘다 → 늘고 있다 (is increasing).", "example_in_sentence": "늘고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "추운 겨울에 할 수 있는 재미있는 활동이거든요.", "translation": "Because it''s a fun activity you can do in the cold winter.", "vocab": [{"ko": "춥다", "en": "to be cold"}, {"ko": "겨울", "en": "winter"}, {"ko": "재미있다", "en": "to be fun; to be interesting"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다 (possibility/ability)", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility. 하다 → 할 수 있다 (can do).", "example_in_sentence": "할 수 있는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present participle / attributive ending)", "exp": "Modifies 활동. 할 수 있다 → 할 수 있는 (that can be done).", "example_in_sentence": "할 수 있는 재미있는 활동"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~거든요", "exp": "Gives a reason or background in a friendly way: ''you see''. 활동이다 → 활동이거든요 (because it''s an activity, you see).", "example_in_sentence": "활동이거든요"}]}, {"text": "이 작품을 본 사람들이 매우 놀랐어요.", "translation": "People who saw this work were very surprised.", "vocab": [{"ko": "작품", "en": "work; artwork"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very"}, {"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 보다 (to see) → 본 사람들 (people who saw).", "example_in_sentence": "본 사람들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks completion of past action/state in polite style. 놀라다 → 놀랐어요 (were surprised).", "example_in_sentence": "놀랐어요"}]}, {"text": "눈으로 이렇게 정교한 모양을 만들 수 있다니 신기해요.", "translation": "It is amazing that such a detailed shape can be made out of snow.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정교하다", "en": "to be detailed; to be intricate"}, {"ko": "모양", "en": "shape; form"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be fascinating"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다 (possibility/ability)", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility. 만들다 → 만들 수 있다 (can make).", "example_in_sentence": "만들 수 있다니"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~다니", "exp": "Shows surprise at a fact: ''to think that ...!'' 만들 수 있다 → 만들 수 있다니 (that you can make it!).", "example_in_sentence": "만들 수 있다니"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요 (present tense, polite)", "exp": "Marks present state/quality in polite style. 신기하다 → 신기해요 (is amazing).", "example_in_sentence": "신기해요"}]}, {"text": "우리나라에서도 겨울마다 눈사람을 만들어요.", "translation": "In our country, people also make snowmen every winter.", "vocab": [{"ko": "우리나라", "en": "our country"}, {"ko": "겨울", "en": "winter"}, {"ko": "눈사람", "en": "snowman"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also/even particle)", "exp": "Marks inclusivity or addition. 우리나라 + 도 (also in our country).", "example_in_sentence": "우리나라에서도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~마다 (every/each time particle)", "exp": "Marks regular recurrence. 겨울 + 마다 (every winter).", "example_in_sentence": "겨울마다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요 (present tense, polite)", "exp": "Marks present habitual action in polite style. 만들다 → 만들어요 (make).", "example_in_sentence": "만들어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 이런 복잡한 도형을 만드는 것은 쉽지 않아요.", "translation": "However, making such complex shapes is not easy.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "but; however"}, {"ko": "복잡하다", "en": "to be complex; to be complicated"}, {"ko": "도형", "en": "shape"}, {"ko": "쉽다", "en": "to be easy"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~는 것 (nominalizer)", "exp": "Converts verb phrase to noun. 만들다 → 만드는 것 (the making/act of making).", "example_in_sentence": "만드는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다 (negation)", "exp": "Negates adjective/verb. 쉽다 → 쉽지 않다 (is not easy).", "example_in_sentence": "쉽지 않아요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "누군가", "en": "someone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "눈", "en": "snow", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도형", "en": "shape", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이", "en": "this", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여러", "en": "several; many", "note": ""}, {"ko": "면", "en": "side; face", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to have", "note": ""}, {"ko": "눈조각상", "en": "snow sculpture", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "점점", "en": "gradually", "note": ""}, {"ko": "춥다", "en": "to be cold", "note": ""}, {"ko": "겨울", "en": "winter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "재미있다", "en": "to be fun; to be interesting", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작품", "en": "work; artwork", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see", "note": ""}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정교하다", "en": "to be detailed; to be intricate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모양", "en": "shape; form", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be fascinating", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우리나라", "en": "our country", "note": ""}, {"ko": "눈사람", "en": "snowman", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "but; however", "note": ""}, {"ko": "복잡하다", "en": "to be complex; to be complicated", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쉽다", "en": "to be easy", "note": ""}, {"word": "다각형", "reading": "dagakhyeong", "meaning": "polygon", "context": "이 도형은 여러 개의 면이 있는 다각형(polygon)이에요"}, {"word": "활동", "reading": "hwaldong", "meaning": "activity; action", "context": "추운 겨울에 할 수 있는 재미있는 활동이거든요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~으로 (instrumental particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks the material or means used to make/create something. 눈 (snow) → 눈으로 (with/out of snow).", "ex_ko": "누군가가 눈으로 특별한 도형을 만들었어요.", "ex_en": "Someone made a special shape out of snow."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks completion of past action/state in polite style. 놀라다 → 놀랐어요 (were surprised).", "ex_ko": "누군가가 눈으로 특별한 도형을 만들었어요.", "ex_en": "Someone made a special shape out of snow."}, {"name": "~는 (present participle / attributive ending)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Modifies 사람들 to indicate the continuous action. 만들다 → 만드는 (that make/making).", "ex_ko": "이 도형은 여러 개의 면이 있는 다각형(polygon)이에요.", "ex_en": "This shape is a polygon with multiple sides."}, {"name": "이에요 (copula, polite present)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Copular verb in polite style. Links subject to predicate noun. 다각형 + 이에요 (is a polygon).", "ex_ko": "이 도형은 여러 개의 면이 있는 다각형(polygon)이에요.", "ex_en": "This shape is a polygon with multiple sides."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (progressive aspect)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Expresses ongoing or continuous action/state. 늘다 → 늘고 있다 (is increasing).", "ex_ko": "눈조각상을 만드는 사람들이 점점 늘고 있어요.", "ex_en": "The number of people making snow sculptures is gradually increasing."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있다 (possibility/ability)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility. 만들다 → 만들 수 있다 (can make).", "ex_ko": "추운 겨울에 할 수 있는 재미있는 활동이거든요.", "ex_en": "Because it''s a fun activity you can do in the cold winter."}, {"name": "~거든요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Gives a reason or background in a friendly way: ''you see''. 활동이다 → 활동이거든요 (because it''s an activity, you see).", "ex_ko": "추운 겨울에 할 수 있는 재미있는 활동이거든요.", "ex_en": "Because it''s a fun activity you can do in the cold winter."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 보다 (to see) → 본 사람들 (people who saw).", "ex_ko": "이 작품을 본 사람들이 매우 놀랐어요.", "ex_en": "People who saw this work were very surprised."}, {"name": "~어요 (present tense, polite)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks present state/quality in polite style. 신기하다 → 신기해요 (is amazing).", "ex_ko": "눈으로 이렇게 정교한 모양을 만들 수 있다니 신기해요.", "ex_en": "It is amazing that such a detailed shape can be made out of snow."}, {"name": "~도 (also/even particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks inclusivity or addition. 우리나라 + 도 (also in our country).", "ex_ko": "우리나라에서도 겨울마다 눈사람을 만들어요.", "ex_en": "In our country, people also make snowmen every winter."}, {"name": "~마다 (every/each time particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks regular recurrence. 겨울 + 마다 (every winter).", "ex_ko": "우리나라에서도 겨울마다 눈사람을 만들어요.", "ex_en": "In our country, people also make snowmen every winter."}, {"name": "~지 않다 (negation)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Negates adjective/verb. 쉽다 → 쉽지 않다 (is not easy).", "ex_ko": "하지만 이런 복잡한 도형을 만드는 것은 쉽지 않아요.", "ex_en": "However, making such complex shapes is not easy."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mon2max0626g' and md5(translation) = '4ebfb16723476c7566104d1df9002ca5';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A person rescued a small bird. The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation.", "After (the bird) was rescued, a surprising thing happened. The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it.", "The bird keeps sitting on top of that person''s hand. It seems as if (it) is expressing a feeling of gratitude.", "This kind of scene is very special and moving. It shows that animals also remember a person''s help and feel grateful."], "sentences": [{"text": "한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.", "translation": "A person rescued a small bird.", "vocab": [{"ko": "구하다", "en": "to save, rescue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마리", "en": "counter for animals", "note": "새 한 마리 = one bird"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past polite ending. 구해 주다 → 구해주었어요 (rescued). Stems with ㅏ/ㅗ take 았; others take 었.", "example_in_sentence": "구해주었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 주다 (do for)", "exp": "do as a favor. 구하다 → 구해 주다 → 구해주었어요 = \"saved (for him/it)\".", "example_in_sentence": "구해주었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 작다 (small) → 작은 새 (a small bird).", "example_in_sentence": "작은 새"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object particle. 새 한 마리 → 새 한 마리를 = \"(rescued) a bird\".", "example_in_sentence": "새 한 마리를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "subject particle. 사람 → 사람이 = \"a person (subject)\".", "example_in_sentence": "한 사람이"}]}, {"text": "새는 다쳤거나 위험한 상황에 있었어요.", "translation": "The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다치다", "en": "to get hurt, injured", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위험하다", "en": "to be dangerous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past polite. 있다 → 있었어요 = \"was / existed\". 다치다 → 다쳤다 = \"got hurt\".", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~거나", "exp": "Means ''or'' between two actions or states. 다치다 → 다쳤거나 (was hurt, or ...).", "example_in_sentence": "다쳤거나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle. 새 → 새는 = \"the bird (as for the bird)\".", "example_in_sentence": "새는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "static location. 상황 → 상황에 = \"in (the) situation\".", "example_in_sentence": "상황에"}]}, {"text": "새를 구해준 후에 놀라운 일이 일어났어요.", "translation": "After he rescued the bird, something surprising happened.", "vocab": [{"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising", "note": "ㅂ-irregular: 놀랍+은 → 놀라운"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen, occur", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past polite. 일어나다 → 일어났어요 = \"happened\". Stem vowel ㅏ + 았 → 났.", "example_in_sentence": "일어났어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object particle. 새 → 새를 = \"(rescued) the bird\".", "example_in_sentence": "새를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "subject particle. 일 → 일이 = \"a thing (subject)\".", "example_in_sentence": "놀라운 일이"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 후에", "exp": "Means ''after doing''. 구해 주다 → 구해준 후에 (after rescuing).", "example_in_sentence": "구해준 후에"}]}, {"text": "작은 새가 구해준 사람의 손을 떠나려고 하지 않아요.", "translation": "The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "손", "en": "hand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떠나다", "en": "to leave", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negation: ''not''. 떠나려고 하다 → 떠나려고 하지 않다 (does not try to leave).", "example_in_sentence": "하지 않아요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고 (intention)", "exp": "intention. 떠나다 → 떠나려고 (하다) = \"intending to leave / trying to leave\".", "example_in_sentence": "떠나려고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 구해 주다 → 구해준 사람 (the person who rescued it).", "example_in_sentence": "구해준 사람"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object particle. 손 → 손을 = \"(does not leave) the hand\".", "example_in_sentence": "손을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "subject particle. 새 → 새가 = \"the bird (subject)\".", "example_in_sentence": "새가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "Shows possession, like ''s. 사람 → 사람의 손 (the person''s hand).", "example_in_sentence": "사람의 손"}]}, {"text": "새는 그 사람의 손 위에 계속 앉아 있어요.", "translation": "The bird keeps sitting on top of that person''s hand.", "vocab": [{"ko": "위", "en": "top, above", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously", "note": ""}, {"ko": "앉다", "en": "to sit", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다 (resultant state)", "exp": "resultant state. 앉다 → 앉아 있다 = \"is sitting (and remains seated)\".", "example_in_sentence": "앉아 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle. 새 → 새는 = \"as for the bird\".", "example_in_sentence": "새는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "location. 위 → 위에 = \"on top of\".", "example_in_sentence": "손 위에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "possessive. 사람 → 사람의 손 = \"the person''s hand\".", "example_in_sentence": "사람의 손"}]}, {"text": "마치 고마운 마음을 표현하는 것 같아요.", "translation": "It seems as if (it) is expressing a feeling of gratitude.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고맙다", "en": "to be thankful", "note": "ㅂ-irregular: 고맙+은 → 고마운"}, {"ko": "마음", "en": "heart, mind", "note": ""}, {"ko": "표현하다", "en": "to express", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object. 마음 → 마음을 = \"(expressing) the feeling\".", "example_in_sentence": "마음을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것 같다", "exp": "Says what something seems to be doing: ''it seems like''. 표현하다 → 표현하는 것 같아요 (seems to be expressing).", "example_in_sentence": "표현하는 것 같아요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "마치 ~ 것 같다", "exp": "마치 adds ''just as if'' to ~는 것 같다: it''s just as if the bird were saying thank you.", "example_in_sentence": "마치 고마운 마음을 표현하는 것 같아요"}]}, {"text": "이런 모습은 매우 특별하고 감동적이에요.", "translation": "This kind of scene is very special and moving.", "vocab": [{"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance, scene", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "감동적", "en": "moving, touching", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)", "exp": "Sino-Korean noun → adjective. 감동 → 감동적 = \"moving, touching\".", "example_in_sentence": "감동적이에요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle. 모습 → 모습은 = \"as for the scene\".", "example_in_sentence": "모습은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Joins two descriptions: ''and''. 특별하다 → 특별하고 (special and ...).", "example_in_sentence": "특별하고"}]}, {"text": "동물도 사람의 도움을 기억하고 고마워한다는 걸 보여줘요.", "translation": "It shows that animals also remember a person''s help and feel grateful.", "vocab": [{"ko": "동물", "en": "animal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도움", "en": "help", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기억하다", "en": "to remember", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고마워하다", "en": "to feel thankful", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object. 도움 → 도움을 = \"(remember) the help\".", "example_in_sentence": "도움을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Joins two actions: ''and''. 기억하다 → 기억하고 (remember and ...).", "example_in_sentence": "기억하고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also)", "exp": "inclusive. 동물 → 동물도 = \"animals, too\".", "example_in_sentence": "동물도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "possessive. 사람 → 사람의 도움 = \"a person''s help\".", "example_in_sentence": "사람의 도움"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는다는 것", "exp": "Turns a statement into ''the fact that ...''. 고마워하다 → 고마워한다는 걸 (that they feel thankful). 걸 is short for 것을.", "example_in_sentence": "고마워한다는 걸"}]}], "version": "s5"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "구하다", "en": "to save, rescue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마리", "en": "counter for animals", "note": "새 한 마리 = one bird"}, {"ko": "다치다", "en": "to get hurt, injured", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위험하다", "en": "to be dangerous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising", "note": "ㅂ-irregular: 놀랍+은 → 놀라운"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen, occur", "note": ""}, {"ko": "손", "en": "hand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떠나다", "en": "to leave", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위", "en": "top, above", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously", "note": ""}, {"ko": "앉다", "en": "to sit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고맙다", "en": "to be thankful", "note": "ㅂ-irregular: 고맙+은 → 고마운"}, {"ko": "마음", "en": "heart, mind", "note": ""}, {"ko": "표현하다", "en": "to express", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance, scene", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "감동적", "en": "moving, touching", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도움", "en": "help", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기억하다", "en": "to remember", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고마워하다", "en": "to feel thankful", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past polite ending. 구해 주다 → 구해주었어요 (rescued). Stems with ㅏ/ㅗ take 았; others take 었.", "ex_ko": "한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.", "ex_en": "A person rescued a small bird."}, {"name": "~아/어 주다 (do for)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "do as a favor. 구하다 → 구해 주다 → 구해주었어요 = \"saved (for him/it)\".", "ex_ko": "한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.", "ex_en": "A person rescued a small bird."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 작다 (small) → 작은 새 (a small bird).", "ex_ko": "한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.", "ex_en": "A person rescued a small bird."}, {"name": "~을/를 (object marker)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "direct object particle. 새 한 마리 → 새 한 마리를 = \"(rescued) a bird\".", "ex_ko": "한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.", "ex_en": "A person rescued a small bird."}, {"name": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "subject particle. 사람 → 사람이 = \"a person (subject)\".", "ex_ko": "한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.", "ex_en": "A person rescued a small bird."}, {"name": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "past polite. 있다 → 있었어요 = \"was / existed\". 다치다 → 다쳤다 = \"got hurt\".", "ex_ko": "새는 다쳤거나 위험한 상황에 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation."}, {"name": "~거나", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Means ''or'' between two actions or states. 다치다 → 다쳤거나 (was hurt, or ...).", "ex_ko": "새는 다쳤거나 위험한 상황에 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation."}, {"name": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "topic particle. 새 → 새는 = \"the bird (as for the bird)\".", "ex_ko": "새는 다쳤거나 위험한 상황에 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation."}, {"name": "~에 (location/time)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "static location. 상황 → 상황에 = \"in (the) situation\".", "ex_ko": "새는 다쳤거나 위험한 상황에 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Negation: ''not''. 떠나려고 하다 → 떠나려고 하지 않다 (does not try to leave).", "ex_ko": "작은 새가 구해준 사람의 손을 떠나려고 하지 않아요.", "ex_en": "The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it."}, {"name": "~(으)려고 (intention)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "intention. 떠나다 → 떠나려고 (하다) = \"intending to leave / trying to leave\".", "ex_ko": "작은 새가 구해준 사람의 손을 떠나려고 하지 않아요.", "ex_en": "The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it."}, {"name": "~의 (possessive)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Shows possession, like ''s. 사람 → 사람의 손 (the person''s hand).", "ex_ko": "작은 새가 구해준 사람의 손을 떠나려고 하지 않아요.", "ex_en": "The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다 (resultant state)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "resultant state. 앉다 → 앉아 있다 = \"is sitting (and remains seated)\".", "ex_ko": "새는 그 사람의 손 위에 계속 앉아 있어요.", "ex_en": "The bird keeps sitting on top of that person''s hand."}, {"name": "~는 것 같다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Says what something seems to be doing: ''it seems like''. 표현하다 → 표현하는 것 같아요 (seems to be expressing).", "ex_ko": "마치 고마운 마음을 표현하는 것 같아요.", "ex_en": "It seems as if (it) is expressing a feeling of gratitude."}, {"name": "~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Sino-Korean noun → adjective. 감동 → 감동적 = \"moving, touching\".", "ex_ko": "이런 모습은 매우 특별하고 감동적이에요.", "ex_en": "This kind of scene is very special and moving."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'monnobjxw88m' and md5(translation) = '46ffc8dfe375be16f1d83377d3f5bc53';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Something amazing happened in the sea. A large humpback whale jumped right next to a boat with people on it.", "People didn''t expect the whale to suddenly appear. The whale jumped high out of the water. The people on the boat were startled.", "People''s reactions were very funny. Some people screamed. Some people tried to take pictures.", "The whale was very big and beautiful. It''s really difficult to see this kind of sight. It was a special moment meeting the whale in the sea."], "sentences": [{"text": "바다에서 신기한 일이 일어났어요.", "translation": "Something amazing happened in the sea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바다", "en": "sea"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be wonderful"}, {"ko": "일", "en": "thing, event"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen, to occur"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 일어나다 (to happen) → 일어났어요 (happened).", "example_in_sentence": "일어났어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "에서", "exp": "Location particle marking where an action takes place.", "example_in_sentence": "바다에서"}]}, {"text": "큰 혹등고래가 사람들이 탄 배 바로 옆에서 점프했어요.", "translation": "A large humpback whale jumped right next to the boat that people were on.", "vocab": [{"ko": "크다", "en": "big, large"}, {"ko": "혹등고래", "en": "humpback whale"}, {"ko": "배", "en": "boat"}, {"ko": "옆", "en": "side, next to"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 크다 (big) → 큰 혹등고래 (a big humpback whale).", "example_in_sentence": "큰 혹등고래"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 타다 (to ride) → 사람들이 탄 배 (the boat people were on).", "example_in_sentence": "사람들이 탄 배"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 점프하다 (to jump) → 점프했어요 (jumped).", "example_in_sentence": "점프했어요"}]}, {"text": "사람들은 고래가 갑자기 나타날 줄 몰랐어요.", "translation": "People did not know that the whale would appear suddenly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사람", "en": "person, people"}, {"ko": "고래", "en": "whale"}, {"ko": "갑자기", "en": "suddenly"}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 줄 몰랐다", "exp": "Means ''didn''t expect that something would happen''. 나타나다 → 나타날 줄 몰랐어요 (didn''t know it would appear).", "example_in_sentence": "나타날 줄 몰랐어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 모르다 is 르-irregular: 모르다 → 몰랐어요 (didn''t know).", "example_in_sentence": "몰랐어요"}]}, {"text": "고래는 물 밖으로 높이 뛰어올랐어요.", "translation": "The whale jumped high out of the water.", "vocab": [{"ko": "물", "en": "water"}, {"ko": "밖", "en": "outside"}, {"ko": "높이", "en": "high (adverb)"}, {"ko": "뛰어오르다", "en": "to jump up"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~으로", "exp": "Direction/goal particle showing movement toward a location. Often used with motion verbs.", "example_in_sentence": "밖으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 뛰어오르다 is 르-irregular: 뛰어오르다 → 뛰어올랐어요 (jumped up).", "example_in_sentence": "뛰어올랐어요"}]}, {"text": "배에 탄 사람들이 깜짝 놀랐어요.", "translation": "The people on the boat were startled.", "vocab": [{"ko": "배", "en": "boat"}, {"ko": "타다", "en": "to ride, to board"}, {"ko": "깜짝", "en": "suddenly, with a start"}, {"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised, to be startled"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 배에 타다 (to get on a boat) → 배에 탄 사람들 (the people on the boat).", "example_in_sentence": "탄 사람들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 놀라다 + 았어요.", "example_in_sentence": "놀랐어요"}]}, {"text": "사람들의 반응이 아주 재미있었어요.", "translation": "People''s reaction was very interesting.", "vocab": [{"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction, response"}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very"}, {"ko": "재미있다", "en": "to be interesting, fun"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive particle indicating ownership or relation. 사람들의 (people''s).", "example_in_sentence": "사람들의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 재미있다 + 었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "재미있었어요"}]}, {"text": "어떤 사람은 소리를 질렀어요.", "translation": "Some people screamed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "어떤", "en": "some, a certain"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person"}, {"ko": "소리", "en": "sound, scream, voice"}, {"ko": "지르다", "en": "to scream, to yell"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object particle marking direct object of verb. 소리 + 를.", "example_in_sentence": "소리를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 지르다 is 르-irregular: 지르다 → 질렀어요 (screamed).", "example_in_sentence": "질렀어요"}]}, {"text": "어떤 사람은 사진을 찍으려고 했어요.", "translation": "Some people tried to take pictures.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph, picture"}, {"ko": "찍다", "en": "to take (photo), to shoot"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고 하다", "exp": "Means ''to try to / intend to''. 찍다 → 찍으려고 했어요 (tried to take).", "example_in_sentence": "찍으려고 했어요"}]}, {"text": "고래는 아주 크고 아름다웠어요.", "translation": "The whale was very big and beautiful.", "vocab": [{"ko": "크다", "en": "big, large"}, {"ko": "아름답다", "en": "to be beautiful"}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending joining two adjectives or clauses. 크다 + 고.", "example_in_sentence": "크고 아름다웠어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 아름답다 is ㅂ-irregular: 아름답다 → 아름다웠어요 (was beautiful).", "example_in_sentence": "아름다웠어요"}]}, {"text": "이런 모습을 보기는 정말 어려워요.", "translation": "It is really hard to see a sight like this.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이런", "en": "such, like this"}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance, sight"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see, to watch"}, {"ko": "어렵다", "en": "to be difficult"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기", "exp": "Nominalization suffix converting verb to noun. 보다 + 기 (the act of seeing).", "example_in_sentence": "보기는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Topic particle emphasizing the subject of comparison or focus. Used after nominalized verb.", "example_in_sentence": "보기는"}]}, {"text": "바다에서 만난 특별한 순간이었어요.", "translation": "It was a special moment encountered in the sea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "만나다", "en": "to meet, to encounter"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "순간", "en": "moment"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 만나다 (to meet) → 바다에서 만난 순간 (a moment we met at sea).", "example_in_sentence": "만난"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이었어요", "exp": "Past tense copula. 이다 + 었어요 (was).", "example_in_sentence": "이었어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "바다", "en": "sea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be wonderful", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일", "en": "thing, event", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen, to occur", "note": ""}, {"ko": "크다", "en": "big, large", "note": ""}, {"ko": "혹등고래", "en": "humpback whale", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배", "en": "boat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "옆", "en": "side, next to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person, people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고래", "en": "whale", "note": ""}, {"ko": "갑자기", "en": "suddenly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "물", "en": "water", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밖", "en": "outside", "note": ""}, {"ko": "높이", "en": "high (adverb)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "뛰어오르다", "en": "to jump up", "note": ""}, {"ko": "타다", "en": "to ride, to board", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깜짝", "en": "suddenly, with a start", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised, to be startled", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction, response", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very", "note": ""}, {"ko": "재미있다", "en": "to be interesting, fun", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어떤", "en": "some, a certain", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소리", "en": "sound, scream, voice", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지르다", "en": "to scream, to yell", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph, picture", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찍다", "en": "to take (photo), to shoot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아름답다", "en": "to be beautiful", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이런", "en": "such, like this", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance, sight", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see, to watch", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어렵다", "en": "to be difficult", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만나다", "en": "to meet, to encounter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "순간", "en": "moment", "note": ""}, {"word": "사진을 찍다", "reading": "sajin-eul jjikda", "meaning": "to take a photograph", "context": "어떤 사람은 사진을 찍으려고 했어요"}, {"word": "점프하다", "reading": "jeompeu-hada", "meaning": "to jump", "context": "큰 혹등고래가 사람들이 탄 배 바로 옆에서 점프했어요"}, {"word": "깜짝 놀라다", "reading": "kkamjjak nollada", "meaning": "to be startled / to be taken aback", "context": "배에 탄 사람들이 깜짝 놀랐어요"}, {"word": "소리를 지르다", "reading": "sori-reul jireuda", "meaning": "to shout / to scream", "context": "어떤 사람은 소리를 질렀어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past tense. 아름답다 is ㅂ-irregular: 아름답다 → 아름다웠어요 (was beautiful).", "ex_ko": "바다에서 신기한 일이 일어났어요.", "ex_en": "Something amazing happened in the sea."}, {"name": "에서", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Location particle marking where an action takes place.", "ex_ko": "바다에서 신기한 일이 일어났어요.", "ex_en": "Something amazing happened in the sea."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 배에 타다 (to get on a boat) → 배에 탄 사람들 (the people on the boat).", "ex_ko": "큰 혹등고래가 사람들이 탄 배 바로 옆에서 점프했어요.", "ex_en": "A large humpback whale jumped right next to the boat that people were on."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 줄 몰랐다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Means ''didn''t expect that something would happen''. 나타나다 → 나타날 줄 몰랐어요 (didn''t know it would appear).", "ex_ko": "사람들은 고래가 갑자기 나타날 줄 몰랐어요.", "ex_en": "People did not know that the whale would appear suddenly."}, {"name": "~으로", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Direction/goal particle showing movement toward a location. Often used with motion verbs.", "ex_ko": "고래는 물 밖으로 높이 뛰어올랐어요.", "ex_en": "The whale jumped high out of the water."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Possessive particle indicating ownership or relation. 사람들의 (people''s).", "ex_ko": "사람들의 반응이 아주 재미있었어요.", "ex_en": "People''s reaction was very interesting."}, {"name": "~을/를", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Object particle marking direct object of verb. 소리 + 를.", "ex_ko": "어떤 사람은 소리를 질렀어요.", "ex_en": "Some people screamed."}, {"name": "~(으)려고 하다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Means ''to try to / intend to''. 찍다 → 찍으려고 했어요 (tried to take).", "ex_ko": "어떤 사람은 사진을 찍으려고 했어요.", "ex_en": "Some people tried to take pictures."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Connective ending joining two adjectives or clauses. 크다 + 고.", "ex_ko": "고래는 아주 크고 아름다웠어요.", "ex_en": "The whale was very big and beautiful."}, {"name": "~기", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Nominalization suffix converting verb to noun. 보다 + 기 (the act of seeing).", "ex_ko": "이런 모습을 보기는 정말 어려워요.", "ex_en": "It is really hard to see a sight like this."}, {"name": "~는", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Topic particle emphasizing the subject of comparison or focus. Used after nominalized verb.", "ex_ko": "이런 모습을 보기는 정말 어려워요.", "ex_en": "It is really hard to see a sight like this."}, {"name": "~이었어요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past tense copula. 이다 + 었어요 (was).", "ex_ko": "바다에서 만난 특별한 순간이었어요.", "ex_en": "It was a special moment encountered in the sea."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'monnov3d4jfu' and md5(translation) = '0e98d72c511ca24ecbd9e5f872ebd34b';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There are soldiers in Ukraine who operate drones. They play a special game during their break time.", "That game is a game called ''Grand Theft Auto 5'' (GTA V). In this game, you can also operate airplanes and helicopters.", "The reason the soldiers play this game is twofold. The first is to make their minds comfortable in the difficult war situation. The second is to continuously practice their piloting skills.", "It''s really interesting that they can both take rest and develop skills through games. It''s also a fascinating thing that reality and virtual reality are connected like this."], "sentences": [{"text": "우크라이나에서 드론을 조종하는 군인들이 있어요.", "translation": "There are soldiers in Ukraine who operate drones.", "vocab": [{"ko": "조종하다", "en": "to operate, to control", "note": ""}, {"ko": "군인", "en": "soldier", "note": ""}, {"ko": "드론", "en": "drone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우크라이나", "en": "Ukraine", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present verb modifier)", "exp": "verb modifying a noun (present). 조종하다 → 조종하는 + 군인들", "example_in_sentence": "조종하는 군인들"}]}, {"text": "이들은 쉬는 시간에 특별한 게임을 해요.", "translation": "They play a special game during their break time.", "vocab": [{"ko": "쉬다", "en": "to rest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "게임", "en": "game", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with an action. 쉬다 (to rest) → 쉬는 시간 (break time, lit. ''time for resting'').", "example_in_sentence": "쉬는 시간"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (time)", "exp": "Marks time: ''at / during''. 쉬는 시간에 = during break time.", "example_in_sentence": "시간에"}]}, {"text": "그 게임은 ''그랜드 테프트 오토 5''(GTA V)라는 게임이에요.", "translation": "That game is a game called ''Grand Theft Auto 5'' (GTA V).", "vocab": [{"ko": "게임", "en": "game", "note": ""}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 게임에서도 비행기나 헬리콥터를 조종할 수 있어요.", "translation": "In this game, too, you can fly airplanes or helicopters.", "vocab": [{"ko": "게임", "en": "game", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비행기", "en": "airplane", "note": ""}, {"ko": "헬리콥터", "en": "helicopter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조종하다", "en": "to operate, to control", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also)", "exp": "inclusive. \"also / too\"", "example_in_sentence": "게임에서도"}]}, {"text": "군인들이 이 게임을 하는 이유는 두 가지예요.", "translation": "The reason the soldiers play this game is twofold.", "vocab": [{"ko": "군인", "en": "soldier", "note": ""}, {"ko": "게임", "en": "game", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가지", "en": "kind, type", "note": ""}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "첫 번째는 힘든 전쟁 상황에서 마음을 편안하게 하기 위해서예요.", "translation": "The first reason is to ease their minds in the hard situation of war.", "vocab": [{"ko": "힘들다", "en": "to be difficult, hard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전쟁", "en": "war", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마음", "en": "mind, heart", "note": ""}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "두 번째는 조종 실력을 계속 연습하기 위해서예요.", "translation": "The second is to continuously practice their piloting skills.", "vocab": [{"ko": "조종", "en": "operation, control", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실력", "en": "skill, ability", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연습하다", "en": "to practice", "note": ""}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "게임을 통해서 휴식도 취하고 실력도 기를 수 있다니 정말 흥미로워요.", "translation": "It''s really interesting that they can both take rest and develop skills through games.", "vocab": [{"ko": "게임", "en": "game", "note": ""}, {"ko": "휴식", "en": "rest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "취하다", "en": "to take", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실력", "en": "skill, ability", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Joins two actions: ''and''. 취하다 → 취하고 (take ... and).", "example_in_sentence": "취하고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 ~도", "exp": "Repeating 도 means ''both ... and ...''. 휴식도 ... 실력도 = both rest and skills.", "example_in_sentence": "휴식도 취하고 실력도"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을 통해서", "exp": "through, by means of", "example_in_sentence": "게임을 통해서"}]}, {"text": "현실과 가상 현실이 이렇게 연결되는 것도 신기한 일이에요.", "translation": "It''s also a fascinating thing that reality and virtual reality are connected like this.", "vocab": [{"ko": "현실", "en": "reality", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가상", "en": "virtual", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연결되다", "en": "to be connected", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be fascinating, amazing", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present verb modifier)", "exp": "verb modifying a noun (present). 연결되다 → 연결되는 + 것", "example_in_sentence": "연결되는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와 (with/and)", "exp": "with / and (formal)", "example_in_sentence": "현실과"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also)", "exp": "inclusive. \"also / too\"", "example_in_sentence": "것도"}]}], "version": "s1"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "조종하다", "en": "to operate, to control", "note": ""}, {"ko": "군인", "en": "soldier", "note": ""}, {"ko": "드론", "en": "drone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우크라이나", "en": "Ukraine", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쉬다", "en": "to rest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "게임", "en": "game", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비행기", "en": "airplane", "note": ""}, {"ko": "헬리콥터", "en": "helicopter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가지", "en": "kind, type", "note": ""}, {"ko": "힘들다", "en": "to be difficult, hard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전쟁", "en": "war", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마음", "en": "mind, heart", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조종", "en": "operation, control", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실력", "en": "skill, ability", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연습하다", "en": "to practice", "note": ""}, {"ko": "휴식", "en": "rest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "취하다", "en": "to take", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현실", "en": "reality", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가상", "en": "virtual", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연결되다", "en": "to be connected", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be fascinating, amazing", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~는 (present verb modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes a noun with an action. 쉬다 (to rest) → 쉬는 시간 (break time, lit. ''time for resting'').", "ex_ko": "우크라이나에서 드론을 조종하는 군인들이 있어요.", "ex_en": "There are soldiers in Ukraine who operate drones."}, {"name": "~에 (time)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks time: ''at / during''. 쉬는 시간에 = during break time.", "ex_ko": "이들은 쉬는 시간에 특별한 게임을 해요.", "ex_en": "They play a special game during their break time."}, {"name": "~도 (also)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "inclusive. \"also / too\"", "ex_ko": "이 게임에서도 비행기나 헬리콥터를 조종할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "In this game, too, you can fly airplanes or helicopters."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Joins two actions: ''and''. 취하다 → 취하고 (take ... and).", "ex_ko": "게임을 통해서 휴식도 취하고 실력도 기를 수 있다니 정말 흥미로워요.", "ex_en": "It''s really interesting that they can both take rest and develop skills through games."}, {"name": "~도 ~도", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Repeating 도 means ''both ... and ...''. 휴식도 ... 실력도 = both rest and skills.", "ex_ko": "게임을 통해서 휴식도 취하고 실력도 기를 수 있다니 정말 흥미로워요.", "ex_en": "It''s really interesting that they can both take rest and develop skills through games."}, {"name": "~과/와 (with/and)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "with / and (formal)", "ex_ko": "현실과 가상 현실이 이렇게 연결되는 것도 신기한 일이에요.", "ex_en": "It''s also a fascinating thing that reality and virtual reality are connected like this."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'monnpfazj581' and md5(translation) = 'b7773d56db92e9cf903e00fa1aef46b5';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There was a big mistake at the Tampa Police Department in the United States. They chose the wrong sign language interpreter at a press conference.", "The police called a woman with a history of fraud as an interpreter. However, this woman didn''t know how to do sign language properly. Her interpretation was completely wrong.", "People with hearing disabilities could not understand the news. This was because the interpreter only made meaningless gestures. People were very angry about this incident.", "This incident shows that we must be more careful when choosing interpreters. Especially when delivering important news, we should use professionals."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국 탬파 경찰서에서 큰 실수가 있었어요.", "translation": "There was a big mistake at the Tampa Police Department in the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "실수", "en": "mistake"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to have"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker indicating an action or state that occurred in the past. 있다 (to exist) → 있었어요 (there was/existed).", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle marking the location where an action or event takes place.", "example_in_sentence": "경찰서에서"}]}, {"text": "기자회견에서 수화(手話) 통역사를 잘못 선택했어요.", "translation": "At a press conference, they chose the wrong sign language interpreter.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기자회견", "en": "press conference"}, {"ko": "수화", "en": "sign language"}, {"ko": "통역사", "en": "interpreter"}, {"ko": "잘못", "en": "incorrectly; wrongly"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 선택하다 (to select) → 선택했어요 (selected).", "example_in_sentence": "선택했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~를/을", "exp": "Accusative object particle marking the direct object of the verb 선택하다 (to select).", "example_in_sentence": "통역사를"}]}, {"text": "경찰은 사기 전과가 있는 여성을 통역사로 불렀어요.", "translation": "The police called a woman with a fraud record as an interpreter.", "vocab": [{"ko": "경찰", "en": "police"}, {"ko": "사기", "en": "fraud; scam"}, {"ko": "전과", "en": "criminal record"}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call; to invite"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun. 있다 → 있는: 사기 전과가 있는 여성 (a woman who has a fraud record).", "example_in_sentence": "있는 여성"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (as)", "exp": "Marks a role: ''as''. 통역사 → 통역사로 (as an interpreter).", "example_in_sentence": "통역사로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 부르다 (to call) → 불렀어요 (called).", "example_in_sentence": "불렀어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 이 여성은 수화를 제대로 할 줄 몰랐어요.", "translation": "However, this woman did not know how to do sign language properly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "제대로", "en": "properly; correctly"}, {"ko": "모르다", "en": "to not know"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 줄 모르다", "exp": "Means ''to not know how to do''. 하다 → 할 줄 몰랐어요 (didn''t know how to do).", "example_in_sentence": "할 줄 몰랐어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 모르다 (to not know) → 몰랐어요 (did not know).", "example_in_sentence": "몰랐어요"}]}, {"text": "그녀가 한 통역은 완전히 엉터리였어요.", "translation": "The interpretation she did was completely nonsensical.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그녀", "en": "she"}, {"ko": "통역", "en": "interpretation; interpreting"}, {"ko": "완전히", "en": "completely; entirely"}, {"ko": "엉터리", "en": "nonsense; nonsensical"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 하다 → 한 통역 (the interpreting she did).", "example_in_sentence": "한 통역"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~였어요/이었어요", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 (to be). After a vowel use 였어요: 엉터리 → 엉터리였어요 (was nonsense).", "example_in_sentence": "엉터리였어요"}]}, {"text": "청각 장애인들은 뉴스를 이해할 수 없었어요.", "translation": "Deaf people could not understand the news.", "vocab": [{"ko": "청각", "en": "hearing; auditory"}, {"ko": "장애인", "en": "person with a disability"}, {"ko": "뉴스", "en": "news"}, {"ko": "이해하다", "en": "to understand"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 없다", "exp": "Means ''cannot''. 이해하다 → 이해할 수 없었어요 (could not understand).", "example_in_sentence": "이해할 수 없었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 없다 (to not exist; cannot) → 없었어요 (could not).", "example_in_sentence": "없었어요"}]}, {"text": "통역사가 의미 없는 손짓만 했기 때문이에요.", "translation": "It was because the interpreter only made meaningless gestures.", "vocab": [{"ko": "의미", "en": "meaning"}, {"ko": "손짓", "en": "gesture; hand motion"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "Gives the reason: ''it''s because ...''. 했다 → 했기 때문이에요 (it''s because he did).", "example_in_sentence": "했기 때문이에요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~만", "exp": "Particle meaning ''only.'' Emphasizes that only meaningless gestures were made, nothing more.", "example_in_sentence": "손짓만"}]}, {"text": "사람들은 이 일에 대해 매우 화가 났어요.", "translation": "People became very angry about this matter.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people"}, {"ko": "일", "en": "matter; thing; incident"}, {"ko": "화", "en": "anger"}, {"ko": "나다", "en": "to arise; to become"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 대해", "exp": "Particle phrase meaning ''about; concerning.'' Indicates the target or object of an emotion or discussion.", "example_in_sentence": "이 일에 대해"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "화가 나다", "exp": "Expression meaning ''to become angry.'' Combines noun 화 (anger) + 나다 (to arise).", "example_in_sentence": "화가 났어요"}]}, {"text": "이 사건은 통역사를 선택할 때 더 조심해야 한다는 것을 보여줘요.", "translation": "This incident shows that one must be more careful when selecting an interpreter.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; event"}, {"ko": "조심하다", "en": "to be careful"}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 때", "exp": "Means ''when''. 선택하다 → 선택할 때 (when choosing).", "example_in_sentence": "선택할 때"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다", "exp": "Modal expression meaning ''must; should; have to.'' 조심하다 (to be careful) → 조심해야 하다 (must be careful).", "example_in_sentence": "조심해야 한다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는다는 것", "exp": "Turns a statement into ''the fact that ...''. 해야 한다 → 해야 한다는 것 (that one must ...).", "example_in_sentence": "해야 한다는 것"}]}, {"text": "특히 중요한 뉴스를 전할 때는 전문가를 써야 해요.", "translation": "Especially when conveying important news, one must use an expert.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; particularly"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important"}, {"ko": "전하다", "en": "to convey; to deliver"}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 중요하다 → 중요한 뉴스 (important news).", "example_in_sentence": "중요한 뉴스"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 때는", "exp": "''When'', with 는 adding emphasis: ''at times when ...''. 전하다 → 전할 때는 (when delivering).", "example_in_sentence": "전할 때는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다", "exp": "Modal expression meaning ''must; should.'' 쓰다 (to use) → 써야 하다 (must use).", "example_in_sentence": "써야 해요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "실수", "en": "mistake", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to have", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기자회견", "en": "press conference", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수화", "en": "sign language", "note": ""}, {"ko": "통역사", "en": "interpreter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잘못", "en": "incorrectly; wrongly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경찰", "en": "police", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사기", "en": "fraud; scam", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전과", "en": "criminal record", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call; to invite", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제대로", "en": "properly; correctly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모르다", "en": "to not know", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그녀", "en": "she", "note": ""}, {"ko": "통역", "en": "interpretation; interpreting", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완전히", "en": "completely; entirely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "엉터리", "en": "nonsense; nonsensical", "note": ""}, {"ko": "청각", "en": "hearing; auditory", "note": ""}, {"ko": "장애인", "en": "person with a disability", "note": ""}, {"ko": "뉴스", "en": "news", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이해하다", "en": "to understand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의미", "en": "meaning", "note": ""}, {"ko": "손짓", "en": "gesture; hand motion", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일", "en": "matter; thing; incident", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화", "en": "anger", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나다", "en": "to arise; to become", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; event", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조심하다", "en": "to be careful", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; particularly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전하다", "en": "to convey; to deliver", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": ""}, {"word": "청각 장애인", "reading": "cheong-gak jang-ae-in", "meaning": "deaf person; hearing-impaired person", "context": "청각 장애인들은 뉴스를 이해할 수 없었어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense marker indicating an action or state that occurred in the past. 있다 (to exist) → 있었어요 (there was/existed).", "ex_ko": "미국 탬파 경찰서에서 큰 실수가 있었어요.", "ex_en": "There was a big mistake at the Tampa Police Department in the United States."}, {"name": "~에서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locative particle marking the location where an action or event takes place.", "ex_ko": "미국 탬파 경찰서에서 큰 실수가 있었어요.", "ex_en": "There was a big mistake at the Tampa Police Department in the United States."}, {"name": "~를/을", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Accusative object particle marking the direct object of the verb 선택하다 (to select).", "ex_ko": "기자회견에서 수화(手話) 통역사를 잘못 선택했어요.", "ex_en": "At a press conference, they chose the wrong sign language interpreter."}, {"name": "~는 (modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes a noun. 있다 → 있는: 사기 전과가 있는 여성 (a woman who has a fraud record).", "ex_ko": "경찰은 사기 전과가 있는 여성을 통역사로 불렀어요.", "ex_en": "The police called a woman with a fraud record as an interpreter."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (as)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks a role: ''as''. 통역사 → 통역사로 (as an interpreter).", "ex_ko": "경찰은 사기 전과가 있는 여성을 통역사로 불렀어요.", "ex_en": "The police called a woman with a fraud record as an interpreter."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 중요하다 → 중요한 뉴스 (important news).", "ex_ko": "그녀가 한 통역은 완전히 엉터리였어요.", "ex_en": "The interpretation she did was completely nonsensical."}, {"name": "~였어요/이었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 (to be). After a vowel use 였어요: 엉터리 → 엉터리였어요 (was nonsense).", "ex_ko": "그녀가 한 통역은 완전히 엉터리였어요.", "ex_en": "The interpretation she did was completely nonsensical."}, {"name": "~만", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Particle meaning ''only.'' Emphasizes that only meaningless gestures were made, nothing more.", "ex_ko": "통역사가 의미 없는 손짓만 했기 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "It was because the interpreter only made meaningless gestures."}, {"name": "~에 대해", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Particle phrase meaning ''about; concerning.'' Indicates the target or object of an emotion or discussion.", "ex_ko": "사람들은 이 일에 대해 매우 화가 났어요.", "ex_en": "People became very angry about this matter."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 때", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''when''. 선택하다 → 선택할 때 (when choosing).", "ex_ko": "이 사건은 통역사를 선택할 때 더 조심해야 한다는 것을 보여줘요.", "ex_en": "This incident shows that one must be more careful when selecting an interpreter."}, {"name": "~아/어야 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Modal expression meaning ''must; should; have to.'' 조심하다 (to be careful) → 조심해야 하다 (must be careful).", "ex_ko": "이 사건은 통역사를 선택할 때 더 조심해야 한다는 것을 보여줘요.", "ex_en": "This incident shows that one must be more careful when selecting an interpreter."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는다는 것", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns a statement into ''the fact that ...''. 해야 한다 → 해야 한다는 것 (that one must ...).", "ex_ko": "이 사건은 통역사를 선택할 때 더 조심해야 한다는 것을 보여줘요.", "ex_en": "This incident shows that one must be more careful when selecting an interpreter."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 때는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''When'', with 는 adding emphasis: ''at times when ...''. 전하다 → 전할 때는 (when delivering).", "ex_ko": "특히 중요한 뉴스를 전할 때는 전문가를 써야 해요.", "ex_en": "Especially when conveying important news, one must use an expert."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'monnq0ljgjv5' and md5(translation) = '5fbd6d601ef312cba2fdeefb199aaa5b';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A photo comparing the appearance of Chinese railways in 1996 and 2022 has become a hot topic. The changes that occurred over 26 years are truly remarkable.", "In 1996, Chinese railways were slow and had outdated facilities. Train stations were also small and inconvenient. Many people had to wait for a long time to board trains.", "However, by 2022, China had become a high-speed rail powerhouse. Trains exceeding 300 kilometers per hour connect the entire country. Train stations have also changed to be large and modern like airports.", "South Korea has also been developing railways since the 1970s. The high-speed rail era opened when KTX (Korean Train eXpress) opened in 2004. The development of transportation is an important indicator showing a country''s growth."], "sentences": [{"text": "1996년과 2022년 중국 철도의 모습을 비교한 사진이 화제가 되고 있어요.", "translation": "Photos comparing the appearance of Chinese railways in 1996 and 2022 are becoming a hot topic.", "vocab": [{"ko": "철도", "en": "railroad"}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance; state"}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic; hot issue"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요 (progressive aspect)", "exp": "Indicates an action or state in progress or currently ongoing. From 있다 + present tense.", "example_in_sentence": "화제가 되고 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 비교하다 → 비교한 사진 (photos that compare).", "example_in_sentence": "비교한 사진"}]}, {"text": "26년 사이에 일어난 변화가 정말 놀랍습니다.", "translation": "The change that occurred over 26 years is truly remarkable.", "vocab": [{"ko": "변화", "en": "change"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; to be remarkable"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~사이에 (during; over the period of)", "exp": "Indicates a time period or interval. Combines 사이 (interval) with locative particle 에.", "example_in_sentence": "26년 사이에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 일어나다 → 일어난 변화 (the change that happened).", "example_in_sentence": "일어난 변화"}]}, {"text": "1996년 중국 철도는 속도가 느리고 시설이 낡았어요.", "translation": "In 1996, Chinese railways were slow and had deteriorated facilities.", "vocab": [{"ko": "속도", "en": "speed"}, {"ko": "시설", "en": "facility"}, {"ko": "낡다", "en": "to be worn out; to be old and shabby"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (coordinate conjunction)", "exp": "Joins two parallel adjectives or clauses. 느리고 시설이 낡았어요 connects two descriptions.", "example_in_sentence": "느리고"}]}, {"text": "기차역도 작고 불편했습니다.", "translation": "Train stations were also small and inconvenient.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기차역", "en": "train station"}, {"ko": "불편하다", "en": "to be inconvenient"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (coordinate conjunction)", "exp": "Connects two parallel adjectives: 작고 and 불편했습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "작고"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 기차를 타기 위해 오랫동안 기다려야 했어요.", "translation": "Many people had to wait for a long time in order to board the train.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사람들", "en": "people (plural)"}, {"ko": "타다", "en": "to board; to ride"}, {"ko": "기다리다", "en": "to wait"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해 (in order to; for the purpose of)", "exp": "Indicates purpose or goal. Nominalized verb 타기 with purposive expression 위해.", "example_in_sentence": "타기 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 했다", "exp": "Means ''had to''. 기다리다 → 기다려야 했어요 (had to wait).", "example_in_sentence": "기다려야 했어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 2022년 중국은 고속철도(빠른 기차) 강국이 되었어요.", "translation": "However, by 2022, China had become a superpower in high-speed rail.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고속철도", "en": "high-speed rail"}, {"ko": "강국", "en": "superpower; strong nation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 되다", "exp": "Means ''to become (something)''. 강국 + 이 되다 → 강국이 되었어요 (became a powerhouse).", "example_in_sentence": "강국이 되었어요"}]}, {"text": "시속 300킬로미터가 넘는 기차가 전국을 연결합니다.", "translation": "Trains exceeding 300 kilometers per hour connect the entire nation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "시속", "en": "speed per hour; km/h"}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to surpass"}, {"ko": "연결하다", "en": "to connect"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (attributive present tense)", "exp": "Present participle modifying noun. 넘는 modifies 기차.", "example_in_sentence": "넘는 기차"}]}, {"text": "기차역도 공항처럼 크고 현대적으로 바뀌었어요.", "translation": "Train stations have also changed to be large and modern like airports.", "vocab": [{"ko": "공항", "en": "airport"}, {"ko": "현대적", "en": "modern; contemporary"}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change; to be transformed"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (coordinate conjunction)", "exp": "Connects parallel adjectives describing changes: 크고 and 현대적으로.", "example_in_sentence": "크고"}]}, {"text": "한국도 1970년대부터 철도를 발전시켜 왔어요.", "translation": "Korea has also been developing railways since the 1970s.", "vocab": [{"ko": "발전시키다", "en": "to develop; to advance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 오다", "exp": "Shows an action that has continued from the past up to now: ''have been doing''. 발전시키다 → 발전시켜 왔어요 (have been developing).", "example_in_sentence": "발전시켜 왔어요"}]}, {"text": "2004년 케이티엑스(KTX)가 개통되면서 고속철도 시대가 열렸습니다.", "translation": "As KTX opened in 2004, the era of high-speed rail began.", "vocab": [{"ko": "개통되다", "en": "to be opened for service"}, {"ko": "시대", "en": "era; age"}, {"ko": "열리다", "en": "to open; to begin"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서", "exp": "Links an event with what happened along with it: ''as''. 개통되다 → 개통되면서 (as it opened).", "example_in_sentence": "개통되면서"}]}, {"text": "교통 발전은 한 나라의 성장을 보여주는 중요한 지표예요.", "translation": "Transportation development is an important indicator showing a nation''s growth.", "vocab": [{"ko": "교통", "en": "transportation; traffic"}, {"ko": "발전", "en": "development; progress"}, {"ko": "성장", "en": "growth"}, {"ko": "지표", "en": "indicator; index"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (attributive present tense)", "exp": "Present participle modifying 지표. 보여주는 describes what the indicator does.", "example_in_sentence": "보여주는 중요한 지표"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "철도", "en": "railroad", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance; state", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic; hot issue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "변화", "en": "change", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; to be remarkable", "note": ""}, {"ko": "속도", "en": "speed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시설", "en": "facility", "note": ""}, {"ko": "낡다", "en": "to be worn out; to be old and shabby", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기차역", "en": "train station", "note": ""}, {"ko": "불편하다", "en": "to be inconvenient", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람들", "en": "people (plural)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "타다", "en": "to board; to ride", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기다리다", "en": "to wait", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고속철도", "en": "high-speed rail", "note": ""}, {"ko": "강국", "en": "superpower; strong nation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시속", "en": "speed per hour; km/h", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to surpass", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연결하다", "en": "to connect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공항", "en": "airport", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현대적", "en": "modern; contemporary", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change; to be transformed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발전시키다", "en": "to develop; to advance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "개통되다", "en": "to be opened for service", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시대", "en": "era; age", "note": ""}, {"ko": "열리다", "en": "to open; to begin", "note": ""}, {"ko": "교통", "en": "transportation; traffic", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발전", "en": "development; progress", "note": ""}, {"ko": "성장", "en": "growth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지표", "en": "indicator; index", "note": ""}, {"word": "화제가 되다", "reading": "hwaje-ga doeda", "meaning": "to become a topic of discussion / become popular", "context": "비교한 사진이 화제가 되고 있어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~고 있어요 (progressive aspect)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Indicates an action or state in progress or currently ongoing. From 있다 + present tense.", "ex_ko": "1996년과 2022년 중국 철도의 모습을 비교한 사진이 화제가 되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Photos comparing the appearance of Chinese railways in 1996 and 2022 are becoming a hot topic."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 일어나다 → 일어난 변화 (the change that happened).", "ex_ko": "1996년과 2022년 중국 철도의 모습을 비교한 사진이 화제가 되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Photos comparing the appearance of Chinese railways in 1996 and 2022 are becoming a hot topic."}, {"name": "~고 (coordinate conjunction)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Joins two parallel adjectives or clauses. 느리고 시설이 낡았어요 connects two descriptions.", "ex_ko": "1996년 중국 철도는 속도가 느리고 시설이 낡았어요.", "ex_en": "In 1996, Chinese railways were slow and had deteriorated facilities."}, {"name": "~기 위해 (in order to; for the purpose of)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Indicates purpose or goal. Nominalized verb 타기 with purposive expression 위해.", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 기차를 타기 위해 오랫동안 기다려야 했어요.", "ex_en": "Many people had to wait for a long time in order to board the train."}, {"name": "~아/어야 했다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''had to''. 기다리다 → 기다려야 했어요 (had to wait).", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 기차를 타기 위해 오랫동안 기다려야 했어요.", "ex_en": "Many people had to wait for a long time in order to board the train."}, {"name": "~이/가 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''to become (something)''. 강국 + 이 되다 → 강국이 되었어요 (became a powerhouse).", "ex_ko": "하지만 2022년 중국은 고속철도(빠른 기차) 강국이 되었어요.", "ex_en": "However, by 2022, China had become a superpower in high-speed rail."}, {"name": "~는 (attributive present tense)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Present participle modifying 지표. 보여주는 describes what the indicator does.", "ex_ko": "시속 300킬로미터가 넘는 기차가 전국을 연결합니다.", "ex_en": "Trains exceeding 300 kilometers per hour connect the entire nation."}, {"name": "~아/어 오다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows an action that has continued from the past up to now: ''have been doing''. 발전시키다 → 발전시켜 왔어요 (have been developing).", "ex_ko": "한국도 1970년대부터 철도를 발전시켜 왔어요.", "ex_en": "Korea has also been developing railways since the 1970s."}, {"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Links an event with what happened along with it: ''as''. 개통되다 → 개통되면서 (as it opened).", "ex_ko": "2004년 케이티엑스(KTX)가 개통되면서 고속철도 시대가 열렸습니다.", "ex_en": "As KTX opened in 2004, the era of high-speed rail began."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'monnqlfqqm9s' and md5(translation) = '2092101c856443e6a27a23ac6c06e86c';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A foreigner read the instruction manual for an oven he bought at home. The manual had a warning that said ''Do not dry your pets in the oven.''", "This person found this warning funny and posted it on the internet. Many people saw this post and laughed.", "In Korea, there are also many strange warnings in instruction manuals for home appliances. There are warnings like ''Do not put a cat in the microwave.''", "Companies write these warnings to prevent accidents. They are worried that someone might actually do such a thing."], "sentences": [{"text": "한 외국인이 집에서 산 오븐의 사용 설명서를 읽었어요.", "translation": "A foreigner read the user manual of an oven bought at home.", "vocab": [{"ko": "외국인", "en": "foreigner"}, {"ko": "오븐", "en": "oven"}, {"ko": "설명서", "en": "manual; instruction"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 사다 (to buy) → 산 오븐 (the oven he bought).", "example_in_sentence": "산 오븐"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive marker)", "exp": "Marks possession or relationship between nouns.", "example_in_sentence": "오븐의 사용 설명서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Regular past tense ending for narrative. 읽다 → 읽었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "읽었어요"}]}, {"text": "설명서에는 ''오븐으로 애완동물을 말리지 마세요''라는 경고가 있었어요.", "translation": "In the manual, there was a warning that said ''Please do not dry pets in the oven.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "애완동물", "en": "pet"}, {"ko": "말리다", "en": "to dry"}, {"ko": "경고", "en": "warning"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "The place particle 에 plus the topic marker 는: ''in (the manual)''. 설명서에는 = in the manual.", "example_in_sentence": "설명서에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 마세요 (imperative negation)", "exp": "Prohibitive form: 말다 (not to do) suffixed to verb stem. 말리다 → 말리지 마세요.", "example_in_sentence": "말리지 마세요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는", "exp": "Gives the content of a noun: ''the warning that says ...''. ''...마세요'' + 라는 경고 = a warning saying ''...''.", "example_in_sentence": "''오븐으로 애완동물을 말리지 마세요''라는 경고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Regular past tense. 있다 → 있었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 사람은 이 경고문이 재미있어서 인터넷에 올렸어요.", "translation": "This person found the warning funny and posted it on the internet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "경고문", "en": "warning message; warning text"}, {"ko": "재미있다", "en": "to be funny; to be amusing"}, {"ko": "올리다", "en": "to upload; to post"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "Gives the reason for the next action. 재미있다 → 재미있어서 (because it was funny).", "example_in_sentence": "재미있어서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Regular past tense. 올리다 → 올렸어요.", "example_in_sentence": "올렸어요"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이 글을 보고 웃었어요.", "translation": "Many people saw this post and laughed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; a lot of"}, {"ko": "웃다", "en": "to laugh"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (sequential/connective ending)", "exp": "Connects two actions in sequence. 보다 → 보고 (look, and then).", "example_in_sentence": "보고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Regular past tense. 웃다 → 웃었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "웃었어요"}]}, {"text": "한국에서도 가전제품 설명서에는 이상한 경고가 많아요.", "translation": "In Korea too, there are many strange warnings in appliance manuals.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가전제품", "en": "home appliance"}, {"ko": "이상하다", "en": "to be strange; to be odd"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (inclusive particle)", "exp": "Inclusive particle meaning ''also; too.'' Adds the subject to a set.", "example_in_sentence": "한국에서도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는 (locative + emphasis)", "exp": "Location marker + emphasis/contrast particle.", "example_in_sentence": "설명서에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 이상하다 → 이상한 경고 (strange warnings).", "example_in_sentence": "이상한 경고"}]}, {"text": "''전자레인지에 고양이를 넣지 마세요'' 같은 경고도 있어요.", "translation": "There are also warnings like ''Do not put a cat in the microwave.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "전자레인지", "en": "microwave (oven)"}, {"ko": "고양이", "en": "cat"}, {"ko": "넣다", "en": "to put; to insert"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 마세요 (imperative negation)", "exp": "Prohibitive form: 말다 affixed to verb stem. 넣다 → 넣지 마세요.", "example_in_sentence": "넣지 마세요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 같은", "exp": "Means ''like; such as'' after a noun or quote. ''...마세요'' 같은 경고 = warnings like ''...''.", "example_in_sentence": "같은 경고도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (inclusive particle)", "exp": "Adds to a set, meaning ''also; too.''", "example_in_sentence": "경고도"}]}, {"text": "회사들은 사고를 방지하기 위해 이런 경고를 써요.", "translation": "Companies write such warnings to prevent accidents.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사고", "en": "accident"}, {"ko": "방지하다", "en": "to prevent"}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to write"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해 (purpose/goal marker)", "exp": "Nominalized verb form (-기) + 위해 (for the purpose of). Expresses intent or goal.", "example_in_sentence": "방지하기 위해"}]}, {"text": "누군가 실제로 그런 일을 할까 봐 걱정하는 거예요.", "translation": "They worry that someone might actually do such a thing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "누군가", "en": "someone"}, {"ko": "실제로", "en": "actually; in reality"}, {"ko": "걱정하다", "en": "to worry"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ까 봐", "exp": "Shows worry that something might happen. 하다 → 할까 봐 (afraid that someone might do it).", "example_in_sentence": "할까 봐"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 거예요", "exp": "Explains the reason or situation: ''it''s that ...''. 걱정하다 → 걱정하는 거예요 (it''s that they worry).", "example_in_sentence": "걱정하는 거예요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "외국인", "en": "foreigner", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오븐", "en": "oven", "note": ""}, {"ko": "설명서", "en": "manual; instruction", "note": ""}, {"ko": "애완동물", "en": "pet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "말리다", "en": "to dry", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경고", "en": "warning", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경고문", "en": "warning message; warning text", "note": ""}, {"ko": "재미있다", "en": "to be funny; to be amusing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "올리다", "en": "to upload; to post", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; a lot of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "웃다", "en": "to laugh", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가전제품", "en": "home appliance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이상하다", "en": "to be strange; to be odd", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전자레인지", "en": "microwave (oven)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고양이", "en": "cat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넣다", "en": "to put; to insert", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사고", "en": "accident", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방지하다", "en": "to prevent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to write", "note": ""}, {"ko": "누군가", "en": "someone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실제로", "en": "actually; in reality", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걱정하다", "en": "to worry", "note": ""}, {"word": "사용 설명서", "reading": "sayong seolmyeong seo", "meaning": "instruction manual; user manual", "context": "오븐의 사용 설명서를 읽었어요"}, {"word": "인터넷", "reading": "inteonet", "meaning": "internet", "context": "인터넷에 올렸어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 이상하다 → 이상한 경고 (strange warnings).", "ex_ko": "한 외국인이 집에서 산 오븐의 사용 설명서를 읽었어요.", "ex_en": "A foreigner read the user manual of an oven bought at home."}, {"name": "~의 (possessive marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks possession or relationship between nouns.", "ex_ko": "한 외국인이 집에서 산 오븐의 사용 설명서를 읽었어요.", "ex_en": "A foreigner read the user manual of an oven bought at home."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Regular past tense ending for narrative. 읽다 → 읽었어요.", "ex_ko": "한 외국인이 집에서 산 오븐의 사용 설명서를 읽었어요.", "ex_en": "A foreigner read the user manual of an oven bought at home."}, {"name": "~에는 (locative + emphasis)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "The place particle 에 plus the topic marker 는: ''in (the manual)''. 설명서에는 = in the manual.", "ex_ko": "설명서에는 ''오븐으로 애완동물을 말리지 마세요''라는 경고가 있었어요.", "ex_en": "In the manual, there was a warning that said ''Please do not dry pets in the oven.''"}, {"name": "~지 마세요 (imperative negation)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Prohibitive form: 말다 (not to do) suffixed to verb stem. 말리다 → 말리지 마세요.", "ex_ko": "설명서에는 ''오븐으로 애완동물을 말리지 마세요''라는 경고가 있었어요.", "ex_en": "In the manual, there was a warning that said ''Please do not dry pets in the oven.''"}, {"name": "~(이)라는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Gives the content of a noun: ''the warning that says ...''. ''...마세요'' + 라는 경고 = a warning saying ''...''.", "ex_ko": "설명서에는 ''오븐으로 애완동물을 말리지 마세요''라는 경고가 있었어요.", "ex_en": "In the manual, there was a warning that said ''Please do not dry pets in the oven.''"}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Gives the reason for the next action. 재미있다 → 재미있어서 (because it was funny).", "ex_ko": "이 사람은 이 경고문이 재미있어서 인터넷에 올렸어요.", "ex_en": "This person found the warning funny and posted it on the internet."}, {"name": "~고 (sequential/connective ending)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connects two actions in sequence. 보다 → 보고 (look, and then).", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 이 글을 보고 웃었어요.", "ex_en": "Many people saw this post and laughed."}, {"name": "~도 (inclusive particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Inclusive particle meaning ''also; too.'' Adds the subject to a set.", "ex_ko": "한국에서도 가전제품 설명서에는 이상한 경고가 많아요.", "ex_en": "In Korea too, there are many strange warnings in appliance manuals."}, {"name": "~ 같은", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''like; such as'' after a noun or quote. ''...마세요'' 같은 경고 = warnings like ''...''.", "ex_ko": "''전자레인지에 고양이를 넣지 마세요'' 같은 경고도 있어요.", "ex_en": "There are also warnings like ''Do not put a cat in the microwave.''"}, {"name": "~기 위해 (purpose/goal marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Nominalized verb form (-기) + 위해 (for the purpose of). Expresses intent or goal.", "ex_ko": "회사들은 사고를 방지하기 위해 이런 경고를 써요.", "ex_en": "Companies write such warnings to prevent accidents."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ까 봐", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows worry that something might happen. 하다 → 할까 봐 (afraid that someone might do it).", "ex_ko": "누군가 실제로 그런 일을 할까 봐 걱정하는 거예요.", "ex_en": "They worry that someone might actually do such a thing."}, {"name": "~는 거예요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Explains the reason or situation: ''it''s that ...''. 걱정하다 → 걱정하는 거예요 (it''s that they worry).", "ex_ko": "누군가 실제로 그런 일을 할까 봐 걱정하는 거예요.", "ex_en": "They worry that someone might actually do such a thing."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'monnrb9840nj' and md5(translation) = '1298f3266e2d5ea40901a322b0b0bf5c';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Recently, a special house has been making headlines on the internet overseas. The unique feature of this house is that a canal passes through the inside of the building.", "Generally, it is natural for a canal to be outside a house. However, this house was designed so that the canal runs through the building.", "This unique architectural method is attracting the attention of many people. There are many reactions saying that the sight of water flowing inside the house is very interesting.", "In Korea, there are also cases of utilizing water channels in traditional houses. However, it is very rare for a canal to directly pass through a house. It makes one curious whether this kind of creative architecture will increase in the future."], "sentences": [{"text": "최근 해외에서 특별한 집이 인터넷에서 화제가 되고 있어요.", "translation": "Recently, a unique house overseas has become a hot topic online.", "vocab": [{"ko": "최근", "en": "recently"}, {"ko": "해외", "en": "overseas"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic of discussion"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "화제가 되다", "exp": "Idiomatic verb phrase meaning ''become a topic/become newsworthy.'' Similar pattern to 이슈가 되다 or 관심을 끌다.", "example_in_sentence": "화제가 되고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "이 집의 특징은 운하가 집 안을 통과한다는 점입니다.", "translation": "What makes this house special is that a canal runs through the inside of it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특징", "en": "characteristic"}, {"ko": "운하", "en": "canal"}, {"ko": "통과하다", "en": "to pass through"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는다는 점", "exp": "Means ''the fact / point that ...''. 통과하다 → 통과한다는 점 (the fact that it passes through).", "example_in_sentence": "통과한다는 점"}]}, {"text": "일반적으로 운하는 집 밖에 있는 것이 당연해요.", "translation": "Generally, it is natural that canals are located outside houses.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일반적으로", "en": "generally"}, {"ko": "당연하다", "en": "to be natural; to be obvious"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것이 당연하다", "exp": "Means ''it is natural that ...''. 있다 → 있는 것이 당연해요 (it''s natural for it to be ...).", "example_in_sentence": "집 밖에 있는 것이 당연해요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 이 집은 운하가 건물을 관통해서 지나가도록 설계되었습니다.", "translation": "However, this house was designed so that the canal runs right through the building.", "vocab": [{"ko": "관통하다", "en": "to pass through; to pierce"}, {"ko": "지나가다", "en": "to pass"}, {"ko": "설계되다", "en": "to be designed"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "Links two actions; the first shows how the second happens. 관통하다 → 관통해서 지나가다 (to go through by cutting across it).", "example_in_sentence": "관통해서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도록", "exp": "Purpose/intention marker meaning ''so that'' or ''in order to.'' Often follows verb or adjective: 지나가다 → 지나가도록 (designed so that it passes).", "example_in_sentence": "지나가도록 설계되었습니다"}]}, {"text": "이런 독특한 건축 방식은 많은 사람들의 관심을 끌고 있어요.", "translation": "This unique architectural method is drawing the attention of many people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "독특하다", "en": "to be unique"}, {"ko": "건축", "en": "architecture; construction"}, {"ko": "방식", "en": "method; way"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "관심을 끌다", "exp": "Fixed phrase: ''to attract attention'' (끌다 = to pull). 관심을 끌고 있어요 (is attracting attention).", "example_in_sentence": "관심을 끌고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "물이 집 안을 흐르는 모습이 매우 신기하다는 반응이 많습니다.", "translation": "There are many reactions saying that the sight of water flowing inside the house is very interesting.", "vocab": [{"ko": "흐르다", "en": "to flow"}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "sight; appearance"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be fascinating"}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction; response"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 모습", "exp": "Noun phrase combining present participle ~는 + 모습 (sight/appearance) to describe visual aspect of action: 흐르다 → 흐르는 모습.", "example_in_sentence": "물이 집 안을 흐르는 모습"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 반응", "exp": "Pattern where ~다는 embeds a clause into noun 반응, meaning ''reactions/responses saying that ~.'' Uses declarative ~다 + 는.", "example_in_sentence": "신기하다는 반응"}]}, {"text": "우리나라에서도 전통 가옥에서 물길을 활용한 사례가 있어요.", "translation": "In our country too, there are cases of utilizing water channels in traditional houses.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전통", "en": "tradition; traditional"}, {"ko": "가옥", "en": "house; dwelling"}, {"ko": "물길", "en": "water channel; waterway"}, {"ko": "활용하다", "en": "to use; to make use of"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 활용하다 → 물길을 활용한 사례 (cases where water channels were used).", "example_in_sentence": "물길을 활용한 사례"}]}, {"text": "하지만 운하가 직접 집을 통과하는 경우는 매우 드문 일입니다.", "translation": "However, it is very rare for a canal to pass directly through a house.", "vocab": [{"ko": "직접", "en": "directly"}, {"ko": "경우", "en": "case; instance"}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "to be rare"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 경우", "exp": "Noun phrase using present participle ~는 + 경우 (case/situation). Relativizes clause: 통과하다 → 통과하는 경우.", "example_in_sentence": "집을 통과하는 경우"}]}, {"text": "이런 창의적인 건축이 앞으로 더 늘어날지 궁금해집니다.", "translation": "It makes me wonder whether this kind of creative architecture will become more common in the future.", "vocab": [{"ko": "창의적", "en": "creative"}, {"ko": "앞으로", "en": "in the future; from now on"}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "to increase"}, {"ko": "궁금하다", "en": "to be curious; to wonder"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ지", "exp": "Forms an indirect question about the future: ''whether ... will''. 늘어나다 → 늘어날지 (whether it will increase).", "example_in_sentence": "늘어날지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다", "exp": "Shows a change of state: ''to become''. 궁금하다 (curious) → 궁금해지다 (to become curious).", "example_in_sentence": "궁금해집니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "최근", "en": "recently", "note": ""}, {"ko": "해외", "en": "overseas", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic of discussion", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특징", "en": "characteristic", "note": ""}, {"ko": "운하", "en": "canal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "통과하다", "en": "to pass through", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일반적으로", "en": "generally", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당연하다", "en": "to be natural; to be obvious", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관통하다", "en": "to pass through; to pierce", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지나가다", "en": "to pass", "note": ""}, {"ko": "설계되다", "en": "to be designed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "독특하다", "en": "to be unique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "건축", "en": "architecture; construction", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방식", "en": "method; way", "note": ""}, {"ko": "흐르다", "en": "to flow", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "sight; appearance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be fascinating", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction; response", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전통", "en": "tradition; traditional", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가옥", "en": "house; dwelling", "note": ""}, {"ko": "물길", "en": "water channel; waterway", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활용하다", "en": "to use; to make use of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "직접", "en": "directly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경우", "en": "case; instance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "to be rare", "note": ""}, {"ko": "창의적", "en": "creative", "note": ""}, {"ko": "앞으로", "en": "in the future; from now on", "note": ""}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "to increase", "note": ""}, {"ko": "궁금하다", "en": "to be curious; to wonder", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~ㄴ/는다는 점", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''the fact / point that ...''. 통과하다 → 통과한다는 점 (the fact that it passes through).", "ex_ko": "이 집의 특징은 운하가 집 안을 통과한다는 점입니다.", "ex_en": "What makes this house special is that a canal runs through the inside of it."}, {"name": "~는 것이 당연하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''it is natural that ...''. 있다 → 있는 것이 당연해요 (it''s natural for it to be ...).", "ex_ko": "일반적으로 운하는 집 밖에 있는 것이 당연해요.", "ex_en": "Generally, it is natural that canals are located outside houses."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Links two actions; the first shows how the second happens. 관통하다 → 관통해서 지나가다 (to go through by cutting across it).", "ex_ko": "하지만 이 집은 운하가 건물을 관통해서 지나가도록 설계되었습니다.", "ex_en": "However, this house was designed so that the canal runs right through the building."}, {"name": "~도록", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Purpose/intention marker meaning ''so that'' or ''in order to.'' Often follows verb or adjective: 지나가다 → 지나가도록 (designed so that it passes).", "ex_ko": "하지만 이 집은 운하가 건물을 관통해서 지나가도록 설계되었습니다.", "ex_en": "However, this house was designed so that the canal runs right through the building."}, {"name": "~는 모습", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Noun phrase combining present participle ~는 + 모습 (sight/appearance) to describe visual aspect of action: 흐르다 → 흐르는 모습.", "ex_ko": "물이 집 안을 흐르는 모습이 매우 신기하다는 반응이 많습니다.", "ex_en": "There are many reactions saying that the sight of water flowing inside the house is very interesting."}, {"name": "~다는 반응", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Pattern where ~다는 embeds a clause into noun 반응, meaning ''reactions/responses saying that ~.'' Uses declarative ~다 + 는.", "ex_ko": "물이 집 안을 흐르는 모습이 매우 신기하다는 반응이 많습니다.", "ex_en": "There are many reactions saying that the sight of water flowing inside the house is very interesting."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 활용하다 → 물길을 활용한 사례 (cases where water channels were used).", "ex_ko": "우리나라에서도 전통 가옥에서 물길을 활용한 사례가 있어요.", "ex_en": "In our country too, there are cases of utilizing water channels in traditional houses."}, {"name": "~는 경우", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Noun phrase using present participle ~는 + 경우 (case/situation). Relativizes clause: 통과하다 → 통과하는 경우.", "ex_ko": "하지만 운하가 직접 집을 통과하는 경우는 매우 드문 일입니다.", "ex_en": "However, it is very rare for a canal to pass directly through a house."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ지", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Forms an indirect question about the future: ''whether ... will''. 늘어나다 → 늘어날지 (whether it will increase).", "ex_ko": "이런 창의적인 건축이 앞으로 더 늘어날지 궁금해집니다.", "ex_en": "It makes me wonder whether this kind of creative architecture will become more common in the future."}, {"name": "~아/어지다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows a change of state: ''to become''. 궁금하다 (curious) → 궁금해지다 (to become curious).", "ex_ko": "이런 창의적인 건축이 앞으로 더 늘어날지 궁금해집니다.", "ex_en": "It makes me wonder whether this kind of creative architecture will become more common in the future."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'monnsagnhism' and md5(translation) = '6283837ef11a169669b316758f8a46c2';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["The Dolomites in northern Italy are one of the most beautiful mountain ranges in the world. The scenery created by high mountains and deep valleys is really wonderful.", "The rocky mountains of the Dolomites have a special color. When the sun rises and sets, the mountains change to pink and orange colors. This phenomenon is called ''Alpenglow''.", "Many tourists come to this place. In summer, people enjoy hiking and trekking, and in winter, they come to ski. It''s also a perfect place for taking photos.", "The Dolomites became a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2009. I really want to see this place, which looks like a work of art created by nature."], "sentences": [{"text": "이탈리아 북부에 있는 돌로미테(Dolomites)는 세계에서 가장 아름다운 산맥 중 하나예요.", "translation": "The Dolomites in northern Italy are one of the most beautiful mountain ranges in the world.", "vocab": [{"ko": "북부", "en": "north; northern part"}, {"ko": "산맥", "en": "mountain range"}, {"ko": "아름답다", "en": "to be beautiful"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 중 하나", "exp": "Means ''one of ...''. 가장 아름다운 산맥 중 하나 = one of the most beautiful mountain ranges.", "example_in_sentence": "산맥 중 하나예요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요/이에요", "exp": "Polite form of 이다 (to be). After a vowel use 예요: 하나 → 하나예요 (is one).", "example_in_sentence": "하나예요"}]}, {"text": "높은 산과 깊은 계곡이 만드는 풍경이 정말 멋져요.", "translation": "The landscape created by tall mountains and deep valleys is truly magnificent.", "vocab": [{"ko": "높다", "en": "to be high; tall"}, {"ko": "계곡", "en": "valley"}, {"ko": "멋지다", "en": "to be great; cool; magnificent"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present participle relative clause)", "exp": "~는 in a relative clause describes an ongoing or habitual action. ''만드는 풍경'' = ''the landscape that [mountains and valleys] make/create''.", "example_in_sentence": "만드는 풍경"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와 (conjunction: and)", "exp": "Connects two nouns in coordination. ''산과 계곡'' = ''mountains and valleys''.", "example_in_sentence": "산과 깊은 계곡"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject particle)", "exp": "Marks the subject. After a consonant use 이: 풍경 → 풍경이.", "example_in_sentence": "풍경이"}]}, {"text": "돌로미테의 바위산들은 특별한 색깔을 가지고 있어요.", "translation": "The rock mountains of the Dolomites have special colors.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바위산", "en": "rocky mountain"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "색깔", "en": "color"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (genitive/possessive marker)", "exp": "Marks possession or attribution. ''돌로미테의 바위산들'' = ''the rock mountains of the Dolomites''.", "example_in_sentence": "돌로미테의 바위산들"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 가지고 있다", "exp": "Means ''to have''. 가지다 (to hold) + ~고 있다 → 가지고 있어요 (they have).", "example_in_sentence": "색깔을 가지고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "해가 뜰 때와 질 때 산이 분홍색과 주황색으로 변해요.", "translation": "When the sun rises and when it sets, the mountains turn pink and orange.", "vocab": [{"ko": "해", "en": "sun"}, {"ko": "뜨다", "en": "to rise; to come up"}, {"ko": "지다", "en": "to set; to go down"}, {"ko": "변하다", "en": "to change; to transform"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 때", "exp": "Means ''when''. 뜨다 → 뜰 때 (when it rises); 지다 → 질 때 (when it sets).", "example_in_sentence": "뜰 때와 질 때"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~와/과", "exp": "Joins two nouns: ''and''. After a vowel use 와: 뜰 때와 질 때 (when it rises and when it sets).", "example_in_sentence": "때와"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (instrumental/transformative marker)", "exp": "Marks the result or target state of transformation. ''분홍색과 주황색으로 변해요'' = ''changes into pink and orange''.", "example_in_sentence": "분홍색과 주황색으로 변해요"}]}, {"text": "이런 현상을 ''알펜글뤼헨''이라고 불러요.", "translation": "This phenomenon is called ''Alpenglow.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon"}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call; to name"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 부르다", "exp": "Says what something is called. ''알펜글뤼헨'' + 이라고 부르다 → to call it ''Alpenglow''.", "example_in_sentence": "''알펜글뤼헨''이라고 불러요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (accusative object marker)", "exp": "Marks the direct object. ''현상을'' = ''the phenomenon [as object of calling]''.", "example_in_sentence": "현상을 ''알펜글뤼헨''"}]}, {"text": "많은 관광객들이 이곳을 찾아와요.", "translation": "Many tourists come to visit this place.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; abundant"}, {"ko": "관광객", "en": "tourist"}, {"ko": "찾아오다", "en": "to come to visit"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject particle)", "exp": "Marks the subject. After a consonant use 이: 관광객들 → 관광객들이.", "example_in_sentence": "관광객들이"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "찾아오다 / 찾아가다 (to come/go to visit)", "exp": "Compound verb: 찾다 (to seek/visit) + 오다 (to come). Means ''to come visit'' with a sense of purposeful arrival.", "example_in_sentence": "찾아와요"}]}, {"text": "여름에는 등산과 하이킹을 즐기고, 겨울에는 스키를 타러 와요.", "translation": "In summer, people enjoy mountain climbing and hiking, and in winter they come to ski.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여름", "en": "summer"}, {"ko": "등산", "en": "mountain climbing; hiking"}, {"ko": "하이킹", "en": "hiking"}, {"ko": "즐기다", "en": "to enjoy"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는 (topic-marking locative)", "exp": "Emphasizes a particular time as the topic. ''여름에는'' = ''as for summer''; ''겨울에는'' = ''as for winter''. Creates contrast between seasons.", "example_in_sentence": "여름에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)러 오다", "exp": "Shows the purpose of coming. 타다 → 스키를 타러 와요 (come to ski).", "example_in_sentence": "타러 와요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (coordinating conjunction)", "exp": "Connects two independent clauses describing parallel or sequential actions. ''즐기고, [와요]'' = ''enjoy and [come]''.", "example_in_sentence": "즐기고, 겨울에는"}]}, {"text": "사진을 찍기에도 완벽한 장소예요.", "translation": "It is also a perfect place for taking photographs.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph; photo"}, {"ko": "찍다", "en": "to take (a photo); to shoot"}, {"ko": "완벽하다", "en": "to be perfect; flawless"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기에", "exp": "Means ''for doing (something)''. 찍다 → 찍기에 완벽한 장소 (a perfect place for taking photos).", "example_in_sentence": "찍기에도 완벽한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (even; also; -wise)", "exp": "Adds emphasis or expands scope. ''찍기에도'' = ''even for photo-taking'' or ''also for photography''.", "example_in_sentence": "찍기에도"}]}, {"text": "돌로미테는 2009년에 유네스코 세계유산이 되었어요.", "translation": "The Dolomites became a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2009.", "vocab": [{"ko": "유네스코", "en": "UNESCO"}, {"ko": "세계유산", "en": "World Heritage Site"}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become; to be"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 되다", "exp": "Means ''to become (something)''. 세계유산 + 이 되다 → 세계유산이 되었어요 (became a World Heritage Site).", "example_in_sentence": "세계유산이 되었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Regular past-tense ending. 되다 → 되었어요. Indicates an action or state change that occurred in the past.", "example_in_sentence": "되었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (temporal marker: in/at)", "exp": "Marks a point in time. ''2009년에'' = ''in the year 2009''.", "example_in_sentence": "2009년에"}]}, {"text": "자연이 만든 예술 작품 같은 이 곳을 꼭 한번 보고 싶어요.", "translation": "I really want to see this place, which is like an artwork made by nature, at least once.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자연", "en": "nature"}, {"ko": "예술", "en": "art"}, {"ko": "작품", "en": "work; artwork; piece"}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same; to resemble; like"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 만들다 drops ㄹ: 자연이 만든 (made by nature).", "example_in_sentence": "자연이 만든"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~같은 (like; resembling; such as)", "exp": "Comparison marker. ''예술 작품 같은'' = ''like an artwork'' or ''resembling an artwork''.", "example_in_sentence": "작품 같은 이 곳"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 싶다", "exp": "Means ''want to do''. 보다 → 보고 싶어요 (want to see).", "example_in_sentence": "보고 싶어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (accusative object marker)", "exp": "Marks the direct object. ''곳을'' = ''this place [as object of wanting to see]''.", "example_in_sentence": "곳을 꼭 한번"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "북부", "en": "north; northern part", "note": ""}, {"ko": "산맥", "en": "mountain range", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아름답다", "en": "to be beautiful", "note": ""}, {"ko": "높다", "en": "to be high; tall", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계곡", "en": "valley", "note": ""}, {"ko": "멋지다", "en": "to be great; cool; magnificent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바위산", "en": "rocky mountain", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "색깔", "en": "color", "note": ""}, {"ko": "해", "en": "sun", "note": ""}, {"ko": "뜨다", "en": "to rise; to come up", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지다", "en": "to set; to go down", "note": ""}, {"ko": "변하다", "en": "to change; to transform", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call; to name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; abundant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관광객", "en": "tourist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찾아오다", "en": "to come to visit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여름", "en": "summer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "등산", "en": "mountain climbing; hiking", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하이킹", "en": "hiking", "note": ""}, {"ko": "즐기다", "en": "to enjoy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph; photo", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찍다", "en": "to take (a photo); to shoot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완벽하다", "en": "to be perfect; flawless", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유네스코", "en": "UNESCO", "note": ""}, {"ko": "세계유산", "en": "World Heritage Site", "note": ""}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become; to be", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature", "note": ""}, {"ko": "예술", "en": "art", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작품", "en": "work; artwork; piece", "note": ""}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same; to resemble; like", "note": ""}, {"word": "유네스코 세계유산", "reading": "yuneskeo segyeyusan", "meaning": "UNESCO World Heritage", "context": "돌로미테는 2009년에 유네스코 세계유산이 되었어요"}, {"word": "예술 작품", "reading": "yesul jakpum", "meaning": "work of art; artwork", "context": "자연이 만든 예술 작품 같은 이 곳을"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~ 중 하나", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''one of ...''. 가장 아름다운 산맥 중 하나 = one of the most beautiful mountain ranges.", "ex_ko": "이탈리아 북부에 있는 돌로미테(Dolomites)는 세계에서 가장 아름다운 산맥 중 하나예요.", "ex_en": "The Dolomites in northern Italy are one of the most beautiful mountain ranges in the world."}, {"name": "~예요/이에요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Polite form of 이다 (to be). After a vowel use 예요: 하나 → 하나예요 (is one).", "ex_ko": "이탈리아 북부에 있는 돌로미테(Dolomites)는 세계에서 가장 아름다운 산맥 중 하나예요.", "ex_en": "The Dolomites in northern Italy are one of the most beautiful mountain ranges in the world."}, {"name": "~는 (present participle relative clause)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "~는 in a relative clause describes an ongoing or habitual action. ''만드는 풍경'' = ''the landscape that [mountains and valleys] make/create''.", "ex_ko": "높은 산과 깊은 계곡이 만드는 풍경이 정말 멋져요.", "ex_en": "The landscape created by tall mountains and deep valleys is truly magnificent."}, {"name": "~과/와 (conjunction: and)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connects two nouns in coordination. ''산과 계곡'' = ''mountains and valleys''.", "ex_ko": "높은 산과 깊은 계곡이 만드는 풍경이 정말 멋져요.", "ex_en": "The landscape created by tall mountains and deep valleys is truly magnificent."}, {"name": "~이/가 (subject particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the subject. After a consonant use 이: 관광객들 → 관광객들이.", "ex_ko": "높은 산과 깊은 계곡이 만드는 풍경이 정말 멋져요.", "ex_en": "The landscape created by tall mountains and deep valleys is truly magnificent."}, {"name": "~의 (genitive/possessive marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks possession or attribution. ''돌로미테의 바위산들'' = ''the rock mountains of the Dolomites''.", "ex_ko": "돌로미테의 바위산들은 특별한 색깔을 가지고 있어요.", "ex_en": "The rock mountains of the Dolomites have special colors."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 때", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''when''. 뜨다 → 뜰 때 (when it rises); 지다 → 질 때 (when it sets).", "ex_ko": "해가 뜰 때와 질 때 산이 분홍색과 주황색으로 변해요.", "ex_en": "When the sun rises and when it sets, the mountains turn pink and orange."}, {"name": "~와/과", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Joins two nouns: ''and''. After a vowel use 와: 뜰 때와 질 때 (when it rises and when it sets).", "ex_ko": "해가 뜰 때와 질 때 산이 분홍색과 주황색으로 변해요.", "ex_en": "When the sun rises and when it sets, the mountains turn pink and orange."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (instrumental/transformative marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the result or target state of transformation. ''분홍색과 주황색으로 변해요'' = ''changes into pink and orange''.", "ex_ko": "해가 뜰 때와 질 때 산이 분홍색과 주황색으로 변해요.", "ex_en": "When the sun rises and when it sets, the mountains turn pink and orange."}, {"name": "~(이)라고 부르다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Says what something is called. ''알펜글뤼헨'' + 이라고 부르다 → to call it ''Alpenglow''.", "ex_ko": "이런 현상을 ''알펜글뤼헨''이라고 불러요.", "ex_en": "This phenomenon is called ''Alpenglow.''"}, {"name": "~을/를 (accusative object marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the direct object. ''곳을'' = ''this place [as object of wanting to see]''.", "ex_ko": "이런 현상을 ''알펜글뤼헨''이라고 불러요.", "ex_en": "This phenomenon is called ''Alpenglow.''"}, {"name": "~에는 (topic-marking locative)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Emphasizes a particular time as the topic. ''여름에는'' = ''as for summer''; ''겨울에는'' = ''as for winter''. Creates contrast between seasons.", "ex_ko": "여름에는 등산과 하이킹을 즐기고, 겨울에는 스키를 타러 와요.", "ex_en": "In summer, people enjoy mountain climbing and hiking, and in winter they come to ski."}, {"name": "~(으)러 오다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows the purpose of coming. 타다 → 스키를 타러 와요 (come to ski).", "ex_ko": "여름에는 등산과 하이킹을 즐기고, 겨울에는 스키를 타러 와요.", "ex_en": "In summer, people enjoy mountain climbing and hiking, and in winter they come to ski."}, {"name": "~고 (coordinating conjunction)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connects two independent clauses describing parallel or sequential actions. ''즐기고, [와요]'' = ''enjoy and [come]''.", "ex_ko": "여름에는 등산과 하이킹을 즐기고, 겨울에는 스키를 타러 와요.", "ex_en": "In summer, people enjoy mountain climbing and hiking, and in winter they come to ski."}, {"name": "~기에", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''for doing (something)''. 찍다 → 찍기에 완벽한 장소 (a perfect place for taking photos).", "ex_ko": "사진을 찍기에도 완벽한 장소예요.", "ex_en": "It is also a perfect place for taking photographs."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'monnsxxmuyd3' and md5(translation) = 'bfd2e5e02a8ede6cbb0d1c8cd63eccbf';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "스위스는 세계에서 유일하게 전체 국민을 대피소에 수용할 수 있는 나라예요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "Switzerland is the only country in the world that can shelter its entire population.", "vocab": [{"ko": "유일하다", "en": "to be the only one; to be unique", "note": "adjectival verb"}, {"ko": "전체", "en": "whole; entire", "note": ""}, {"ko": "국민", "en": "citizens; the people (of a nation)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대피소", "en": "shelter; evacuation shelter", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Means ''can''. 수용하다 (to accommodate) → 수용할 수 있는 나라 (a country that can accommodate).", "example_in_sentence": "수용할 수 있는"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "세계에서 유일하게", "exp": "uniquely in the world / the only one globally", "example_in_sentence": "세계에서 유일하게"}]}, {"text": "약 37만 개의 대피소를 운영하고 있습니다.", "idx": 1, "translation": "It operates approximately 370,000 shelters.", "vocab": [{"ko": "약", "en": "approximately; about", "note": ""}, {"ko": "개", "en": "counter for objects", "note": ""}, {"ko": "운영하다", "en": "to operate; to run", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "is doing / ongoing action or state", "example_in_sentence": "운영하고 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "이 대피소들은 완벽한 시설을 갖추고 있어요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "These shelters are equipped with perfect facilities.", "vocab": [{"ko": "완벽하다", "en": "to be perfect; to be complete", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시설", "en": "facility; facilities", "note": ""}, {"ko": "갖추다", "en": "to be equipped with; to have", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (lasting state)", "exp": "With verbs like 갖추다, ~고 있다 describes a lasting state. 갖추다 → 갖추고 있어요 (are equipped with).", "example_in_sentence": "갖추고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "공기 정화 시스템(Air Filtration System), 화장실, 침대, 음식과 물 공급 시설, 전력 발전기까지 모든 것이 준비되어 있습니다.", "idx": 3, "translation": "Air Filtration System, bathrooms, beds, food and water supply facilities, and even power generators—everything is prepared.", "vocab": [{"ko": "화장실", "en": "bathroom; toilet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "침대", "en": "bed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "음식", "en": "food", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발전기", "en": "generator", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지", "exp": "At the end of a list it means ''even''. ... 전력 발전기까지 = even power generators.", "example_in_sentence": "발전기까지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다", "exp": "Shows a state that remains after an action. 준비되다 → 준비되어 있습니다 (is ready).", "example_in_sentence": "준비되어 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "스위스의 이런 준비는 국가 안전을 위한 오랜 정책의 결과예요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "This preparedness in Switzerland is the result of a long-standing policy for national security.", "vocab": [{"ko": "준비", "en": "preparation; preparedness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정책", "en": "policy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결과", "en": "result; outcome", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 위한", "exp": "Means ''for (the sake of)'' before a noun. 국가 안전을 위한 정책 (a policy for national security).", "example_in_sentence": "국가 안전을 위한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 결과 (particle ~의 for possession/relation)", "exp": "result of / outcome of", "example_in_sentence": "정책의 결과예요"}]}, {"text": "비상시에 모든 국민이 안전하게 대피할 수 있도록 만든 것입니다.", "idx": 5, "translation": "It was made so that all citizens can evacuate safely in case of emergency.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비상시", "en": "emergency; time of emergency", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있도록", "exp": "Means ''so that (someone) can''. 대피하다 → 대피할 수 있도록 (so that they can evacuate).", "example_in_sentence": "대피할 수 있도록"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것이다", "exp": "Explains the purpose or background: ''it is that ...''. 만들다 → 만든 것입니다 (it was built (so that ...)).", "example_in_sentence": "만든 것입니다"}]}, {"text": "한국도 지하철역이나 지하 공간을 대피소로 활용할 수 있어요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "Korea can also utilize subway stations or underground spaces as shelters.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지하철역", "en": "subway station", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지하 공간", "en": "underground space", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활용하다", "en": "to use; to make use of", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다 (can / be able to)", "exp": "can / is able to", "example_in_sentence": "활용할 수 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)나", "exp": "Means ''or'' between nouns. 지하철역이나 지하 공간 (subway stations or underground spaces).", "example_in_sentence": "지하철역이나 지하 공간"}]}, {"text": "하지만 스위스처럼 전 국민을 수용할 수 있는 규모는 아닙니다.", "idx": 7, "translation": "However, it is not on a scale that can shelter the whole population, as Switzerland can.", "vocab": [{"ko": "규모", "en": "scale; size", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있는", "exp": "Means ''that can ...'' before a noun. 수용하다 → 수용할 수 있는 규모 (a scale that can accommodate).", "example_in_sentence": "수용할 수 있는 규모"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 아니다", "exp": "Negative of 이다: ''is not''. 는 adds contrast: 규모는 아닙니다 (it is not on that scale).", "example_in_sentence": "규모는 아닙니다"}]}, {"text": "스위스의 철저한 대비는 세계적으로 주목받고 있어요.", "idx": 8, "translation": "Switzerland''s thorough preparation is drawing attention globally.", "vocab": [{"ko": "철저하다", "en": "to be thorough; to be meticulous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대비", "en": "preparation; readiness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주목받다", "en": "to draw attention; to be in the spotlight", "note": "passive of 주목하다"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 철저하다 → 철저한 대비 (thorough preparation).", "example_in_sentence": "철저한 대비"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~적으로", "exp": "Turns a ~적 word into an adverb. 세계적 (global) → 세계적으로 (globally; around the world).", "example_in_sentence": "세계적으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Shows an ongoing action: ''is ...ing''. 주목받다 → 주목받고 있어요 (is drawing attention).", "example_in_sentence": "주목받고 있어요"}]}], "version": "s1"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "유일하다", "en": "to be the only one; to be unique", "note": "adjectival verb"}, {"ko": "전체", "en": "whole; entire", "note": ""}, {"ko": "국민", "en": "citizens; the people (of a nation)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대피소", "en": "shelter; evacuation shelter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "약", "en": "approximately; about", "note": ""}, {"ko": "개", "en": "counter for objects", "note": ""}, {"ko": "운영하다", "en": "to operate; to run", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완벽하다", "en": "to be perfect; to be complete", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시설", "en": "facility; facilities", "note": ""}, {"ko": "갖추다", "en": "to be equipped with; to have", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화장실", "en": "bathroom; toilet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "침대", "en": "bed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "음식", "en": "food", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발전기", "en": "generator", "note": ""}, {"ko": "준비", "en": "preparation; preparedness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정책", "en": "policy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결과", "en": "result; outcome", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비상시", "en": "emergency; time of emergency", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지하철역", "en": "subway station", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지하 공간", "en": "underground space", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활용하다", "en": "to use; to make use of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "규모", "en": "scale; size", "note": ""}, {"ko": "철저하다", "en": "to be thorough; to be meticulous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대비", "en": "preparation; readiness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주목받다", "en": "to draw attention; to be in the spotlight", "note": "passive of 주목하다"}, {"ko": "수용하다", "en": "accommodate, house", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정화하다", "en": "purify, filter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공급하다", "en": "supply, provide", "note": ""}, {"ko": "준비하다", "en": "prepare, get ready", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대피하다", "en": "evacuate, take refuge", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "safe, secure", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공간", "en": "space, area", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''can''. 수용하다 (to accommodate) → 수용할 수 있는 나라 (a country that can accommodate).", "ex_ko": "스위스는 세계에서 유일하게 전체 국민을 대피소에 수용할 수 있는 나라예요.", "ex_en": "Switzerland is the only country in the world that can shelter its entire population."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (lasting state)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "With verbs like 갖추다, ~고 있다 describes a lasting state. 갖추다 → 갖추고 있어요 (are equipped with).", "ex_ko": "약 37만 개의 대피소를 운영하고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "It operates approximately 370,000 shelters."}, {"name": "~까지", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "At the end of a list it means ''even''. ... 전력 발전기까지 = even power generators.", "ex_ko": "공기 정화 시스템(Air Filtration System), 화장실, 침대, 음식과 물 공급 시설, 전력 발전기까지 모든 것이 준비되어 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Air Filtration System, bathrooms, beds, food and water supply facilities, and even power generators—everything is prepared."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows a state that remains after an action. 준비되다 → 준비되어 있습니다 (is ready).", "ex_ko": "공기 정화 시스템(Air Filtration System), 화장실, 침대, 음식과 물 공급 시설, 전력 발전기까지 모든 것이 준비되어 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Air Filtration System, bathrooms, beds, food and water supply facilities, and even power generators—everything is prepared."}, {"name": "~을/를 위한", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''for (the sake of)'' before a noun. 국가 안전을 위한 정책 (a policy for national security).", "ex_ko": "스위스의 이런 준비는 국가 안전을 위한 오랜 정책의 결과예요.", "ex_en": "This preparedness in Switzerland is the result of a long-standing policy for national security."}, {"name": "~의 결과 (particle ~의 for possession/relation)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "result of / outcome of", "ex_ko": "스위스의 이런 준비는 국가 안전을 위한 오랜 정책의 결과예요.", "ex_en": "This preparedness in Switzerland is the result of a long-standing policy for national security."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있도록", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''so that (someone) can''. 대피하다 → 대피할 수 있도록 (so that they can evacuate).", "ex_ko": "비상시에 모든 국민이 안전하게 대피할 수 있도록 만든 것입니다.", "ex_en": "It was made so that all citizens can evacuate safely in case of emergency."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 것이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Explains the purpose or background: ''it is that ...''. 만들다 → 만든 것입니다 (it was built (so that ...)).", "ex_ko": "비상시에 모든 국민이 안전하게 대피할 수 있도록 만든 것입니다.", "ex_en": "It was made so that all citizens can evacuate safely in case of emergency."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있다 (can / be able to)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "can / is able to", "ex_ko": "한국도 지하철역이나 지하 공간을 대피소로 활용할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Korea can also utilize subway stations or underground spaces as shelters."}, {"name": "~(이)나", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''or'' between nouns. 지하철역이나 지하 공간 (subway stations or underground spaces).", "ex_ko": "한국도 지하철역이나 지하 공간을 대피소로 활용할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Korea can also utilize subway stations or underground spaces as shelters."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''that can ...'' before a noun. 수용하다 → 수용할 수 있는 규모 (a scale that can accommodate).", "ex_ko": "하지만 스위스처럼 전 국민을 수용할 수 있는 규모는 아닙니다.", "ex_en": "However, it is not on a scale that can shelter the whole population, as Switzerland can."}, {"name": "~은/는 아니다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Negative of 이다: ''is not''. 는 adds contrast: 규모는 아닙니다 (it is not on that scale).", "ex_ko": "하지만 스위스처럼 전 국민을 수용할 수 있는 규모는 아닙니다.", "ex_en": "However, it is not on a scale that can shelter the whole population, as Switzerland can."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 철저하다 → 철저한 대비 (thorough preparation).", "ex_ko": "스위스의 철저한 대비는 세계적으로 주목받고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Switzerland''s thorough preparation is drawing attention globally."}, {"name": "~적으로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns a ~적 word into an adverb. 세계적 (global) → 세계적으로 (globally; around the world).", "ex_ko": "스위스의 철저한 대비는 세계적으로 주목받고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Switzerland''s thorough preparation is drawing attention globally."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'monntk35uaxb' and md5(translation) = 'f56528f3a9aefbc3501ca5a07c0fd2c8';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A young girl living in Lopburi, Thailand carries a special item with her. It''s a fake gun. This gun is not a real gun but a toy gun.", "The girl has a reason for carrying this fake gun. It''s because of monkeys. There are many monkeys living in Lopburi.", "These monkeys frequently take people''s food. The girl carries a fake gun to protect her food. The monkeys get scared and don''t take the food.", "Lopburi, Thailand is a city famous for its monkeys. Many tourists come to see the monkeys. However, for local residents it sometimes becomes a problem."], "sentences": [{"text": "태국 롭부리에 사는 어린 소녀가 특별한 물건을 들고 다녀요.", "translation": "A young girl living in Lopburi, Thailand carries a special object.", "vocab": [{"ko": "롭부리", "en": "Lopburi (city in Thailand)"}, {"ko": "어리다", "en": "to be young"}, {"ko": "소녀", "en": "girl"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a present action. 살다 drops ㄹ: 살다 → 롭부리에 사는 소녀 (a girl who lives in Lopburi).", "example_in_sentence": "롭부리에 사는 어린 소녀"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 다니다", "exp": "Auxiliary verb 다니다 after connector ~고. Indicates habitual or continuous action of 들다 (carry/hold). 들다 → 들고 다니다.", "example_in_sentence": "물건을 들고 다녀요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Polite present ending. 다니다 → 다녀요.", "example_in_sentence": "다녀요"}]}, {"text": "바로 가짜 총이에요.", "translation": "It is a fake gun.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바로", "en": "right, precisely"}, {"ko": "가짜", "en": "fake"}, {"ko": "총", "en": "gun"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요", "exp": "Copula (이다) in polite present tense (-이에요). Used after consonant-final nouns. 이다 → 이에요.", "example_in_sentence": "가짜 총이에요"}]}, {"text": "이 총은 진짜 총이 아니라 장난감 총이에요.", "translation": "This gun is not a real gun but a toy gun.", "vocab": [{"ko": "진짜", "en": "real"}, {"ko": "아니다", "en": "not to be"}, {"ko": "장난감", "en": "toy"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 아니라", "exp": "Means ''not A but B''. 진짜 총이 아니라 장난감 총 (not a real gun but a toy gun).", "example_in_sentence": "진짜 총이 아니라 장난감 총"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은", "exp": "Topic-marking particle after consonant-final noun. Identifies subject of statement.", "example_in_sentence": "이 총은"}]}, {"text": "소녀가 이 가짜 총을 가지고 다니는 이유가 있어요.", "translation": "There is a reason why the girl carries this fake gun.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가지다", "en": "to have, to carry"}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist, to have"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Present tense modifier attached to 다니다 (carry habitually). Creates relative clause modifying 이유.", "example_in_sentence": "가지고 다니는 이유"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 있어요", "exp": "Says that something exists: ''there is''. 이유 + 가 있어요 → there is a reason.", "example_in_sentence": "이유가 있어요"}]}, {"text": "바로 원숭이 때문이에요.", "translation": "It is because of monkeys.", "vocab": [{"ko": "원숭이", "en": "monkey"}, {"ko": "때문", "en": "because of; reason"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 때문이다", "exp": "After a noun it means ''it is because of ...''. 원숭이 때문이에요 (it''s because of the monkeys).", "example_in_sentence": "원숭이 때문이에요"}]}, {"text": "롭부리에는 원숭이가 많이 살아요.", "translation": "Many monkeys live in Lopburi.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많이", "en": "a lot, much"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "Locative particle ~에 + topic marker ~는. Indicates location with emphasis or contrast.", "example_in_sentence": "롭부리에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. 살다 → 살아요.", "example_in_sentence": "살아요"}]}, {"text": "이 원숭이들은 사람들의 음식을 자주 가져가요.", "translation": "These monkeys often take people''s food.", "vocab": [{"ko": "원숭이", "en": "monkey"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person"}, {"ko": "음식", "en": "food"}, {"ko": "자주", "en": "often"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~들", "exp": "Plural suffix. Marks plural noun. 원숭이 → 원숭이들.", "example_in_sentence": "원숭이들은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive particle. Links possessor 사람들 to possessed object 음식.", "example_in_sentence": "사람들의 음식"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. 가져가다 → 가져가요.", "example_in_sentence": "가져가요"}]}, {"text": "소녀는 자신의 음식을 지키려고 가짜 총을 들고 다녀요.", "translation": "The girl carries a fake gun in order to protect her own food.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself, one''s own"}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to protect, to guard"}, {"ko": "들다", "en": "to carry, to hold"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고", "exp": "Shows the purpose of an action: ''in order to''. 지키다 → 지키려고 (in order to protect).", "example_in_sentence": "지키려고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 다니다", "exp": "Auxiliary verb 다니다 after ~고. Indicates continuous habitual action. 들다 → 들고 다니다.", "example_in_sentence": "총을 들고 다녀요"}]}, {"text": "원숭이들이 무서워해서 음식을 가져가지 않아요.", "translation": "The monkeys are scared of it, so they don''t take the food.", "vocab": [{"ko": "무서워하다", "en": "to be scared, to be afraid"}, {"ko": "가져가다", "en": "to take away"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "Causal/sequential connector. 무서워하다 → 무서워해서. Links reason (fear) to result (not taking).", "example_in_sentence": "무서워해서 음식을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negative form. 가져가다 → 가져가지 않다 → 가져가지 않아요. Negates action.", "example_in_sentence": "가져가지 않아요"}]}, {"text": "태국 롭부리는 원숭이로 유명한 도시예요.", "translation": "Lopburi, Thailand is a city famous for monkeys.", "vocab": [{"ko": "유명하다", "en": "to be famous"}, {"ko": "도시", "en": "city"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 유명하다", "exp": "Means ''famous for ...''. 원숭이로 유명한 도시 (a city famous for monkeys).", "example_in_sentence": "원숭이로 유명한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 유명하다 (famous) → 유명한 도시 (a famous city).", "example_in_sentence": "유명한 도시"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요", "exp": "Copula in polite present tense after vowel-final noun. 이다 → 예요.", "example_in_sentence": "도시예요"}]}, {"text": "많은 관광객들이 원숭이를 보러 와요.", "translation": "Many tourists come to see monkeys.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be a lot"}, {"ko": "관광객", "en": "tourist"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see, to watch"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 많다 (many) → 많은 관광객들 (many tourists).", "example_in_sentence": "많은 관광객들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)러 오다", "exp": "Shows the purpose of coming. 보다 (to see) → 보러 와요 (come to see).", "example_in_sentence": "보러 와요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. 오다 → 와요.", "example_in_sentence": "와요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 지역 주민들에게는 때때로 문제가 되기도 해요.", "translation": "However, it sometimes becomes a problem for local residents.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "but, however"}, {"ko": "지역", "en": "area, region"}, {"ko": "주민", "en": "resident"}, {"ko": "때때로", "en": "sometimes, occasionally"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게는", "exp": "Means ''for / to (someone)'', with 는 adding contrast. 주민들에게는 = for the residents (though).", "example_in_sentence": "주민들에게는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 되다", "exp": "Means ''to become (something)''. 문제가 되다 = to become a problem.", "example_in_sentence": "문제가 되기"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기도 하다", "exp": "Auxiliary expressing possibility/occasional occurrence. Attached to gerund form. 되다 → 되기도 해요.", "example_in_sentence": "되기도 해요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "롭부리", "en": "Lopburi (city in Thailand)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어리다", "en": "to be young", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소녀", "en": "girl", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바로", "en": "right, precisely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가짜", "en": "fake", "note": ""}, {"ko": "총", "en": "gun", "note": ""}, {"ko": "진짜", "en": "real", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아니다", "en": "not to be", "note": ""}, {"ko": "장난감", "en": "toy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가지다", "en": "to have, to carry", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist, to have", "note": ""}, {"ko": "원숭이", "en": "monkey", "note": ""}, {"ko": "때문", "en": "because of; reason", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많이", "en": "a lot, much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "음식", "en": "food", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자주", "en": "often", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself, one''s own", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to protect, to guard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "들다", "en": "to carry, to hold", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무서워하다", "en": "to be scared, to be afraid", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가져가다", "en": "to take away", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유명하다", "en": "to be famous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도시", "en": "city", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be a lot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관광객", "en": "tourist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see, to watch", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "but, however", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지역", "en": "area, region", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주민", "en": "resident", "note": ""}, {"ko": "때때로", "en": "sometimes, occasionally", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~는 (verb modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes a noun with a present action. 살다 drops ㄹ: 살다 → 롭부리에 사는 소녀 (a girl who lives in Lopburi).", "ex_ko": "태국 롭부리에 사는 어린 소녀가 특별한 물건을 들고 다녀요.", "ex_en": "A young girl living in Lopburi, Thailand carries a special object."}, {"name": "~고 다니다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Auxiliary verb 다니다 after connector ~고. Indicates habitual or continuous action of 들다 (carry/hold). 들다 → 들고 다니다.", "ex_ko": "태국 롭부리에 사는 어린 소녀가 특별한 물건을 들고 다녀요.", "ex_en": "A young girl living in Lopburi, Thailand carries a special object."}, {"name": "~아/어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. 가져가다 → 가져가요.", "ex_ko": "태국 롭부리에 사는 어린 소녀가 특별한 물건을 들고 다녀요.", "ex_en": "A young girl living in Lopburi, Thailand carries a special object."}, {"name": "~이에요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Copula (이다) in polite present tense (-이에요). Used after consonant-final nouns. 이다 → 이에요.", "ex_ko": "바로 가짜 총이에요.", "ex_en": "It is a fake gun."}, {"name": "~이/가 아니라", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''not A but B''. 진짜 총이 아니라 장난감 총 (not a real gun but a toy gun).", "ex_ko": "이 총은 진짜 총이 아니라 장난감 총이에요.", "ex_en": "This gun is not a real gun but a toy gun."}, {"name": "~은", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Topic-marking particle after consonant-final noun. Identifies subject of statement.", "ex_ko": "이 총은 진짜 총이 아니라 장난감 총이에요.", "ex_en": "This gun is not a real gun but a toy gun."}, {"name": "~이/가 있어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Says that something exists: ''there is''. 이유 + 가 있어요 → there is a reason.", "ex_ko": "소녀가 이 가짜 총을 가지고 다니는 이유가 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a reason why the girl carries this fake gun."}, {"name": "~ 때문이다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "After a noun it means ''it is because of ...''. 원숭이 때문이에요 (it''s because of the monkeys).", "ex_ko": "바로 원숭이 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "It is because of monkeys."}, {"name": "~에는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locative particle ~에 + topic marker ~는. Indicates location with emphasis or contrast.", "ex_ko": "롭부리에는 원숭이가 많이 살아요.", "ex_en": "Many monkeys live in Lopburi."}, {"name": "~들", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Plural suffix. Marks plural noun. 원숭이 → 원숭이들.", "ex_ko": "이 원숭이들은 사람들의 음식을 자주 가져가요.", "ex_en": "These monkeys often take people''s food."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Possessive particle. Links possessor 사람들 to possessed object 음식.", "ex_ko": "이 원숭이들은 사람들의 음식을 자주 가져가요.", "ex_en": "These monkeys often take people''s food."}, {"name": "~(으)려고", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows the purpose of an action: ''in order to''. 지키다 → 지키려고 (in order to protect).", "ex_ko": "소녀는 자신의 음식을 지키려고 가짜 총을 들고 다녀요.", "ex_en": "The girl carries a fake gun in order to protect her own food."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Causal/sequential connector. 무서워하다 → 무서워해서. Links reason (fear) to result (not taking).", "ex_ko": "원숭이들이 무서워해서 음식을 가져가지 않아요.", "ex_en": "The monkeys are scared of it, so they don''t take the food."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Negative form. 가져가다 → 가져가지 않다 → 가져가지 않아요. Negates action.", "ex_ko": "원숭이들이 무서워해서 음식을 가져가지 않아요.", "ex_en": "The monkeys are scared of it, so they don''t take the food."}, {"name": "~(으)로 유명하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''famous for ...''. 원숭이로 유명한 도시 (a city famous for monkeys).", "ex_ko": "태국 롭부리는 원숭이로 유명한 도시예요.", "ex_en": "Lopburi, Thailand is a city famous for monkeys."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'monnu5qv2u76' and md5(translation) = '2320602895e16bb34716aa27f890d41c';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["The sea otter is a cute animal that lives in the ocean. Although they live floating on water, they know a special way to keep from drifting away.", "Sea otters wrap kelp around their bodies. They wrap themselves in kelp just like a blanket. Doing this allows them to stay safely on the ocean surface.", "They also use kelp when eating food and when sleeping. They use the kelp like an anchor to stay in one place. This way, they don''t drift away due to waves or ocean currents.", "I think this behavior of sea otters is really clever. It''s a great example showing the wisdom of animals living in nature. Sea otters are intelligent animals that make good use of their natural environment."], "sentences": [{"text": "바다수달(Sea Otter)은 바다에서 사는 귀여운 동물이에요.", "translation": "The sea otter is a cute animal that lives in the sea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바다수달", "en": "sea otter", "note": "Compound noun: 바다(sea) + 수달(otter)"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이들은 물에 떠서 생활하지만 떠내려가지 않는 특별한 방법을 알고 있어요.", "translation": "These animals float on water but know a special way not to drift away.", "vocab": [{"ko": "뜨다", "en": "to float", "note": "~서 combines two actions in sequence"}, {"ko": "떠내려가다", "en": "to drift away", "note": "Compound verb: 떠(float) + 내려가다(go down)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지만", "exp": "Expresses contrast between two clauses", "example_in_sentence": "물에 떠서 생활하지만 떠내려가지 않는"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "바다수달은 다시마를 자신의 몸에 감아요.", "translation": "The sea otter wraps kelp around its own body.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다시마", "en": "kelp", "note": "Type of marine plant"}, {"ko": "감다", "en": "to wrap around; to wind", "note": "Can mean to roll, wrap, or wind something"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "마치 담요처럼 다시마로 몸을 둘러싸는 거예요.", "translation": "It wraps its body with kelp like a blanket.", "vocab": [{"ko": "담요", "en": "blanket", "note": "Used here as a comparison with 마치"}, {"ko": "둘러싸다", "en": "to surround; to wrap around", "note": "Similar to 감다 but implies surrounding completely"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "마치 ~처럼", "exp": "Expresses similarity or comparison: ''just like'' or ''as if''", "example_in_sentence": "마치 담요처럼 다시마로 몸을 둘러싸는"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이렇게 하면 바다 위에서 안전하게 있을 수 있어요.", "translation": "This way, it can stay safe on the sea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe", "note": "Adverb form of 안전하다(safe)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~으면", "exp": "Conditional: ''if/when'' expressing result of previous action", "example_in_sentence": "이렇게 하면 바다 위에서 안전하게 있을"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "먹이를 먹을 때나 잠을 잘 때도 다시마를 이용해요.", "translation": "When eating food or sleeping, it also uses kelp.", "vocab": [], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을 때나 ~을 때도", "exp": "Multiple time expressions with 나 (or) and 도 (also): ''both when...and when...''", "example_in_sentence": "먹이를 먹을 때나 잠을 잘 때도"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "다시마를 닻처럼 사용해서 한 곳에 머물러 있어요.", "translation": "It uses kelp like an anchor to stay in one place.", "vocab": [{"ko": "닻", "en": "anchor", "note": "Nautical term; used metaphorically here"}, {"ko": "머무르다", "en": "to stay; to remain", "note": "~어 있다 shows continuous state"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~처럼 사용해서", "exp": "Shows manner and connects to result: ''by using like...''", "example_in_sentence": "닻처럼 사용해서 한 곳에 머물러 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그러면 파도나 바닷물에 떠내려가지 않아요.", "translation": "Then it doesn''t drift away in waves or ocean currents.", "vocab": [{"ko": "파도", "en": "wave", "note": "Ocean/sea waves"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~나", "exp": "Lists multiple items: ''or''", "example_in_sentence": "파도나 바닷물에"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이런 바다수달의 행동은 정말 똑똑하다고 생각해요.", "translation": "I think this behavior of sea otters is really smart.", "vocab": [{"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior; action", "note": "Can refer to physical actions or behavioral patterns"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~다고 생각하다", "exp": "Expresses one''s opinion or thought: ''think that...''", "example_in_sentence": "정말 똑똑하다고 생각해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "자연 속에서 살아가는 동물들의 지혜를 보여주는 좋은 예시예요.", "translation": "It is a good example showing the wisdom of animals living in nature.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지혜", "en": "wisdom", "note": "Abstract noun for knowledge and intelligence"}, {"ko": "예시", "en": "example", "note": "More formal than 예; often used in explanations"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 것", "exp": "Nominalizes a clause; ''(the act of) showing...''", "example_in_sentence": "지혜를 보여주는 좋은 예시"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "바다수달은 자연을 잘 활용하는 영리한 동물이에요.", "translation": "The sea otter is a clever animal that makes good use of nature.", "vocab": [{"ko": "활용하다", "en": "to use; to make use of", "note": "More formal than 쓰다; implies effective usage"}, {"ko": "영리하다", "en": "to be clever; to be smart", "note": "Describes cunning intelligence or smartness"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "바다수달", "en": "sea otter", "note": "Compound noun: 바다(sea) + 수달(otter)"}, {"ko": "뜨다", "en": "to float", "note": "~서 combines two actions in sequence"}, {"ko": "떠내려가다", "en": "to drift away", "note": "Compound verb: 떠(float) + 내려가다(go down)"}, {"ko": "다시마", "en": "kelp", "note": "Type of marine plant"}, {"ko": "감다", "en": "to wrap around; to wind", "note": "Can mean to roll, wrap, or wind something"}, {"ko": "담요", "en": "blanket", "note": "Used here as a comparison with 마치"}, {"ko": "둘러싸다", "en": "to surround; to wrap around", "note": "Similar to 감다 but implies surrounding completely"}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe", "note": "Adverb form of 안전하다(safe)"}, {"ko": "닻", "en": "anchor", "note": "Nautical term; used metaphorically here"}, {"ko": "머무르다", "en": "to stay; to remain", "note": "~어 있다 shows continuous state"}, {"ko": "파도", "en": "wave", "note": "Ocean/sea waves"}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior; action", "note": "Can refer to physical actions or behavioral patterns"}, {"ko": "지혜", "en": "wisdom", "note": "Abstract noun for knowledge and intelligence"}, {"ko": "예시", "en": "example", "note": "More formal than 예; often used in explanations"}, {"ko": "활용하다", "en": "to use; to make use of", "note": "More formal than 쓰다; implies effective usage"}, {"ko": "영리하다", "en": "to be clever; to be smart", "note": "Describes cunning intelligence or smartness"}, {"word": "머물다", "reading": "meomul-da", "meaning": "to stay; to remain in a place", "context": "다시마를 닻처럼 사용해서 한 곳에 머물러 있어요."}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mopumlh00rf2' and md5(translation) = '617e9c4e1b0e7e2dd8f0b33bfc384331';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Fish in the aquarium are watching television. All the fish are looking at the screen in the same way.", "The fish are not moving and staying still. They seem to be concentrating on the television. It''s a really amazing sight.", "People were surprised when they saw this. They learned that fish can also watch television.", "At the aquarium, they make sure the fish don''t get bored. When they show television to the fish, they become more active."], "sentences": [{"text": "수족관에 있는 물고기들이 텔레비전을 보고 있어요.", "translation": "Fish in the aquarium are watching television.", "vocab": [{"ko": "수족관", "en": "aquarium"}, {"ko": "물고기", "en": "fish"}, {"ko": "텔레비전", "en": "television"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to watch; to look at"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (descriptive relative clause modifier)", "exp": "Modifies the noun 물고기들, describing fish that exist in the aquarium. 있다 → 있는.", "example_in_sentence": "있는 물고기들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요 (progressive aspect)", "exp": "Indicates an ongoing or habitual action. 보다 → 보고 있다 → 보고 있어요 (polite present).", "example_in_sentence": "보고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "모든 물고기가 화면을 똑같이 바라보고 있어요.", "translation": "All fish are looking at the screen in the same way.", "vocab": [{"ko": "모든", "en": "all; every"}, {"ko": "화면", "en": "screen"}, {"ko": "똑같이", "en": "identically; in the same way"}, {"ko": "바라보다", "en": "to gaze at; to look at"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요 (progressive aspect)", "exp": "Describes ongoing action of looking. 바라보다 → 바라보고 있다 → 바라보고 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "바라보고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "물고기들은 움직이지 않고 가만히 있어요.", "translation": "The fish are not moving and staying still.", "vocab": [{"ko": "움직이다", "en": "to move"}, {"ko": "가만히", "en": "still; quietly; motionless"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to be; to exist; to stay"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않고 (negation + connective)", "exp": "Negates an action and connects to the following clause. 움직이다 → 움직이지 않다 → 움직이지 않고.", "example_in_sentence": "움직이지 않고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Polite present ending. 있다 → 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}, {"text": "텔레비전에 집중하고 있는 것 같아요.", "translation": "It seems the fish are concentrating on the television.", "vocab": [{"ko": "집중하다", "en": "to concentrate; to focus"}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to seem; to appear; to look like"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있는 (progressive relative clause)", "exp": "Modifies the noun 것, describing an ongoing state. 집중하다 → 집중하고 있다 → 집중하고 있는.", "example_in_sentence": "집중하고 있는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것 같다", "exp": "Means ''it seems like ...''. 집중하고 있다 → 집중하고 있는 것 같아요 (it seems they are concentrating).", "example_in_sentence": "집중하고 있는 것 같아요"}]}, {"text": "정말 신기한 모습이에요.", "translation": "It is a really amazing sight.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정말", "en": "really; very"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be wonderful; to be surprising"}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "sight; appearance; look"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 신기하다 (amazing) → 신기한 모습 (an amazing sight).", "example_in_sentence": "신기한 모습"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "이에요 (copula, polite present)", "exp": "Polite copula ending for nominal predicate. Attaches to noun 모습.", "example_in_sentence": "모습이에요"}]}, {"text": "사람들은 이 모습을 보고 놀랐어요.", "translation": "People saw this sight and were surprised.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people"}, {"ko": "이", "en": "this"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see; to watch"}, {"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised; to be amazed"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (conjunctive, sequential action)", "exp": "Connects two actions in sequence: seeing and then being surprised. 보다 → 보고.", "example_in_sentence": "보고 놀랐어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (polite past tense)", "exp": "Past tense in polite form. 놀라다 → 놀랐다 → 놀랐어요.", "example_in_sentence": "놀랐어요"}]}, {"text": "물고기도 텔레비전을 볼 수 있다는 것을 알게 되었어요.", "translation": "People came to know that fish can also watch television.", "vocab": [{"ko": "알다", "en": "to know; to learn"}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become; to come to"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다 (ability/possibility)", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility. 보다 → 볼 수 있다 (can watch).", "example_in_sentence": "볼 수 있다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 것 (nominalization with quoted content)", "exp": "Nominalizes a clause by adding ~다는 것; the clause 물고기도 텔레비전을 볼 수 있다 becomes the object of 알다.", "example_in_sentence": "볼 수 있다는 것을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다 (come to; come to be)", "exp": "Expresses a transition to a new state or realization. 알다 → 알게 되다 → 알게 되었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "알게 되었어요"}]}, {"text": "수족관에서는 물고기들이 지루하지 않도록 해요.", "translation": "In the aquarium, they make sure fish do not get bored.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지루하다", "en": "to be bored; to be tedious"}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do; to make"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않도록 하다 (prevent/ensure that not)", "exp": "Expresses prevention or ensuring that something does not happen. 지루하다 → 지루하지 않도록 하다.", "example_in_sentence": "지루하지 않도록 해요"}]}, {"text": "텔레비전을 보여주면 물고기들이 더 활발해져요.", "translation": "If you show television to the fish, they become more active.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show (to someone)"}, {"ko": "활발하다", "en": "to be active; to be lively"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "Means ''if / when''. After a vowel just add 면: 보여주다 → 보여주면 (if you show).", "example_in_sentence": "보여주면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (become, inchoative)", "exp": "Inchoative auxiliary expressing change of state: becoming active. 활발하다 → 활발해지다 → 활발해져요.", "example_in_sentence": "활발해져요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "수족관", "en": "aquarium", "note": ""}, {"ko": "물고기", "en": "fish", "note": ""}, {"ko": "텔레비전", "en": "television"