ecomes the object of 알다.", "ex_ko": "물고기도 텔레비전을 볼 수 있다는 것을 알게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "People came to know that fish can also watch television."}, {"name": "~게 되다 (come to; come to be)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Expresses a transition to a new state or realization. 알다 → 알게 되다 → 알게 되었어요.", "ex_ko": "물고기도 텔레비전을 볼 수 있다는 것을 알게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "People came to know that fish can also watch television."}, {"name": "~지 않도록 하다 (prevent/ensure that not)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Expresses prevention or ensuring that something does not happen. 지루하다 → 지루하지 않도록 하다.", "ex_ko": "수족관에서는 물고기들이 지루하지 않도록 해요.", "ex_en": "In the aquarium, they make sure fish do not get bored."}, {"name": "~(으)면", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Means ''if / when''. After a vowel just add 면: 보여주다 → 보여주면 (if you show).", "ex_ko": "텔레비전을 보여주면 물고기들이 더 활발해져요.", "ex_en": "If you show television to the fish, they become more active."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mopun5a155bt' and md5(translation) = 'd8fafd62aa3fec4737f44cde6bdbda85';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Horses are famous for being animals that eat grass. But did you know that sometimes they also eat small animals? This is a phenomenon observed worldwide.", "The reason horses eat meat is because of nutritional deficiency. This behavior appears especially when they lack minerals like protein or sodium. In such situations, horses eat small animals like birds or mice.", "Similar cases have been reported on Jeju Island in Korea. Horses raised on farms there occasionally show this behavior. Experts explain that this is a natural instinct.", "Horses'' main diet is still grass and hay. However, when they lack necessary nutrients, they look for other food. This can be seen as one of the survival instincts of horses."], "sentences": [{"text": "말은 풀을 먹는 동물로 유명해요.", "translation": "Horses are famous as animals that eat grass.", "vocab": [{"ko": "풀", "en": "grass"}, {"ko": "유명하다", "en": "to be famous"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 유명하다", "exp": "Means ''famous as / for ...''. 풀을 먹는 동물로 유명해요 (famous as animals that eat grass).", "example_in_sentence": "동물로 유명해요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 때로는 작은 동물들을 먹기도 한다는 사실을 아시나요?", "translation": "But did you know that horses sometimes eat small animals too?", "vocab": [{"ko": "때로는", "en": "sometimes"}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small"}, {"ko": "사실", "en": "fact"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기도 하다", "exp": "Means ''also / sometimes do''. 먹다 → 먹기도 하다 (sometimes also eat).", "example_in_sentence": "먹기도 한다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는다는 사실", "exp": "Means ''the fact that ...''. 먹기도 하다 → 먹기도 한다는 사실 (the fact that they sometimes eat).", "example_in_sentence": "한다는 사실"}]}, {"text": "이는 전 세계적으로 관찰되는 현상이에요.", "translation": "This is a phenomenon observed worldwide.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전 세계적으로", "en": "worldwide; globally"}, {"ko": "관찰되다", "en": "to be observed"}, {"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a present action. 관찰되다 (to be observed) → 관찰되는 현상 (a phenomenon that is observed).", "example_in_sentence": "관찰되는 현상"}]}, {"text": "말이 고기를 먹는 이유는 영양소가 부족하기 때문이에요.", "translation": "The reason horses eat meat is that they lack nutrients.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이유", "en": "reason"}, {"ko": "영양소", "en": "nutrient"}, {"ko": "부족하다", "en": "to be lacking; to be insufficient"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "Gives the reason: ''it''s because ...''. 부족하다 → 부족하기 때문이에요 (it''s because they lack).", "example_in_sentence": "부족하기 때문이에요"}]}, {"text": "특히 단백질이나 나트륨 같은 미네랄이 부족할 때 나타나는 행동이에요.", "translation": "It is a behavior that appears especially when they lack protein or minerals such as sodium.", "vocab": [{"ko": "단백질", "en": "protein"}, {"ko": "나트륨", "en": "sodium"}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 같은", "exp": "Means ''such as; like'' after a noun. 나트륨 같은 미네랄 (minerals such as sodium).", "example_in_sentence": "나트륨 같은 미네랄"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 때", "exp": "Means ''when''. 부족하다 → 부족할 때 (when they lack).", "example_in_sentence": "부족할 때"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a present action. 나타나다 (to appear) → 나타나는 행동 (a behavior that appears).", "example_in_sentence": "나타나는 행동"}]}, {"text": "이런 상황에서 말들은 작은 새나 쥐 같은 동물을 먹어요.", "translation": "In such situations, horses eat small animals like birds or mice.", "vocab": [{"ko": "상황", "en": "situation; circumstance"}, {"ko": "새", "en": "bird"}, {"ko": "쥐", "en": "mouse; rat"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~(이)나", "exp": "Means ''or'' between nouns. 새나 쥐 (birds or mice).", "example_in_sentence": "새나 쥐"}]}, {"text": "한국의 제주도에서도 비슷한 사례가 보고된 적이 있어요.", "translation": "Similar cases have also been reported in Jeju Island, Korea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "제주도", "en": "Jeju Island"}, {"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "to be similar"}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "case; example"}, {"ko": "보고되다", "en": "to be reported"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 적이 있다", "exp": "Means ''has happened before''. 보고되다 → 보고된 적이 있어요 (has been reported before).", "example_in_sentence": "보고된 적이 있어요"}]}, {"text": "목장에서 기르는 말들이 가끔 이런 행동을 보인다고 해요.", "translation": "It is said that horses raised on farms sometimes show this behavior.", "vocab": [{"ko": "목장", "en": "farm; ranch"}, {"ko": "기르다", "en": "to raise; to rear"}, {"ko": "가끔", "en": "occasionally; sometimes"}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to show; to display"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a present action. 기르다 (to raise) → 기르는 말들 (horses that people raise).", "example_in_sentence": "기르는 말들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는다고 하다", "exp": "Reports what others say: ''they say that ...''. 보이다 → 보인다고 해요 (they say they show).", "example_in_sentence": "보인다고 해요"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 이것이 자연스러운 본능이라고 설명해요.", "translation": "Experts explain that this is a natural instinct.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist"}, {"ko": "자연스럽다", "en": "to be natural"}, {"ko": "본능", "en": "instinct"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 자연스럽다 is ㅂ-irregular: 자연스럽다 → 자연스러운 본능 (a natural instinct).", "example_in_sentence": "자연스러운 본능"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 설명하다", "exp": "Reports an explanation: ''explain that it is ...''. 본능 + 이라고 설명해요 (explain that it is an instinct).", "example_in_sentence": "본능이라고 설명해요"}]}, {"text": "말의 주식은 여전히 풀과 건초예요.", "translation": "Horses'' staple food is still grass and hay.", "vocab": [{"ko": "주식", "en": "staple food; main diet"}, {"ko": "여전히", "en": "still"}, {"ko": "건초", "en": "hay"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "하지만 필요한 영양소가 부족하면 다른 음식을 찾게 돼요.", "translation": "However, if necessary nutrients are lacking, they end up looking for other food.", "vocab": [{"ko": "필요하다", "en": "to be necessary; to need"}, {"ko": "음식", "en": "food"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find; to look for"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 필요하다 (necessary) → 필요한 영양소 (necessary nutrients).", "example_in_sentence": "필요한 영양소"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "Means ''if''. 부족하다 → 부족하면 (if they lack).", "example_in_sentence": "부족하면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "Means ''to end up doing / come to do''. 찾다 → 찾게 돼요 (end up looking for).", "example_in_sentence": "찾게 돼요"}]}, {"text": "이는 말의 생존 본능 중 하나라고 볼 수 있어요.", "translation": "This can be seen as one of horses'' survival instincts.", "vocab": [{"ko": "생존", "en": "survival"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 중 하나", "exp": "Means ''one of ...''. 생존 본능 중 하나 (one of their survival instincts).", "example_in_sentence": "본능 중 하나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 볼 수 있다", "exp": "Means ''it can be seen as ...''. 하나 + 라고 볼 수 있어요 (can be seen as one).", "example_in_sentence": "하나라고 볼 수 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "풀", "en": "grass", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유명하다", "en": "to be famous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "때로는", "en": "sometimes", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사실", "en": "fact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전 세계적으로", "en": "worldwide; globally", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관찰되다", "en": "to be observed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영양소", "en": "nutrient", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부족하다", "en": "to be lacking; to be insufficient", "note": ""}, {"ko": "단백질", "en": "protein", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나트륨", "en": "sodium", "note": ""}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation; circumstance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "새", "en": "bird", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쥐", "en": "mouse; rat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제주도", "en": "Jeju Island", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "to be similar", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "case; example", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보고되다", "en": "to be reported", "note": ""}, {"ko": "목장", "en": "farm; ranch", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기르다", "en": "to raise; to rear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가끔", "en": "occasionally; sometimes", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to show; to display", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자연스럽다", "en": "to be natural", "note": ""}, {"ko": "본능", "en": "instinct", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주식", "en": "staple food; main diet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여전히", "en": "still", "note": ""}, {"ko": "건초", "en": "hay", "note": ""}, {"ko": "필요하다", "en": "to be necessary; to need", "note": ""}, {"ko": "음식", "en": "food", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find; to look for", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생존", "en": "survival", "note": ""}, {"word": "풀을 먹다", "reading": "pul-eul meok-da", "meaning": "to eat grass; to graze", "context": "말은 풀을 먹는 동물로 유명해요"}, {"word": "미네랄", "reading": "mi-ne-ral", "meaning": "mineral", "context": "단백질이나 나트륨 같은 미네랄이 부족할 때"}, {"word": "나타나다", "reading": "na-ta-na-da", "meaning": "to appear; to emerge; to manifest", "context": "미네랄이 부족할 때 나타나는 행동이에요"}, {"word": "생존 본능", "reading": "saeng-jon bon-neung", "meaning": "survival instinct", "context": "말의 생존 본능 중 하나라고 볼 수 있어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)로 유명하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''famous as / for ...''. 풀을 먹는 동물로 유명해요 (famous as animals that eat grass).", "ex_ko": "말은 풀을 먹는 동물로 유명해요.", "ex_en": "Horses are famous as animals that eat grass."}, {"name": "~기도 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''also / sometimes do''. 먹다 → 먹기도 하다 (sometimes also eat).", "ex_ko": "하지만 때로는 작은 동물들을 먹기도 한다는 사실을 아시나요?", "ex_en": "But did you know that horses sometimes eat small animals too?"}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는다는 사실", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''the fact that ...''. 먹기도 하다 → 먹기도 한다는 사실 (the fact that they sometimes eat).", "ex_ko": "하지만 때로는 작은 동물들을 먹기도 한다는 사실을 아시나요?", "ex_en": "But did you know that horses sometimes eat small animals too?"}, {"name": "~는 (verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes a noun with a present action. 관찰되다 (to be observed) → 관찰되는 현상 (a phenomenon that is observed).", "ex_ko": "이는 전 세계적으로 관찰되는 현상이에요.", "ex_en": "This is a phenomenon observed worldwide."}, {"name": "~기 때문이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Gives the reason: ''it''s because ...''. 부족하다 → 부족하기 때문이에요 (it''s because they lack).", "ex_ko": "말이 고기를 먹는 이유는 영양소가 부족하기 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "The reason horses eat meat is that they lack nutrients."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 때", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''when''. 부족하다 → 부족할 때 (when they lack).", "ex_ko": "특히 단백질이나 나트륨 같은 미네랄이 부족할 때 나타나는 행동이에요.", "ex_en": "It is a behavior that appears especially when they lack protein or minerals such as sodium."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 적이 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''has happened before''. 보고되다 → 보고된 적이 있어요 (has been reported before).", "ex_ko": "한국의 제주도에서도 비슷한 사례가 보고된 적이 있어요.", "ex_en": "Similar cases have also been reported in Jeju Island, Korea."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는다고 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports what others say: ''they say that ...''. 보이다 → 보인다고 해요 (they say they show).", "ex_ko": "목장에서 기르는 말들이 가끔 이런 행동을 보인다고 해요.", "ex_en": "It is said that horses raised on farms sometimes show this behavior."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a word that describes a noun. 자연스럽다 is ㅂ-irregular: 자연스럽다 → 자연스러운 본능 (a natural instinct).", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이것이 자연스러운 본능이라고 설명해요.", "ex_en": "Experts explain that this is a natural instinct."}, {"name": "~(이)라고 설명하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports an explanation: ''explain that it is ...''. 본능 + 이라고 설명해요 (explain that it is an instinct).", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이것이 자연스러운 본능이라고 설명해요.", "ex_en": "Experts explain that this is a natural instinct."}, {"name": "~(으)면", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''if''. 부족하다 → 부족하면 (if they lack).", "ex_ko": "하지만 필요한 영양소가 부족하면 다른 음식을 찾게 돼요.", "ex_en": "However, if necessary nutrients are lacking, they end up looking for other food."}, {"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''to end up doing / come to do''. 찾다 → 찾게 돼요 (end up looking for).", "ex_ko": "하지만 필요한 영양소가 부족하면 다른 음식을 찾게 돼요.", "ex_en": "However, if necessary nutrients are lacking, they end up looking for other food."}, {"name": "~ 중 하나", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''one of ...''. 생존 본능 중 하나 (one of their survival instincts).", "ex_ko": "이는 말의 생존 본능 중 하나라고 볼 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "This can be seen as one of horses'' survival instincts."}, {"name": "~(이)라고 볼 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''it can be seen as ...''. 하나 + 라고 볼 수 있어요 (can be seen as one).", "ex_ko": "이는 말의 생존 본능 중 하나라고 볼 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "This can be seen as one of horses'' survival instincts."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mopunpuyngx2' and md5(translation) = 'f7af1570ea6150843a64ed7a40b981a3';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["During the American Civil War in 1865, the Union Army attacked South Carolina. This state was the first place to secede from the Union in America.", "The Union Army thought that South Carolina had started the Civil War. So when they arrived in this region, they took great revenge.", "In particular, the Charleston area suffered severe damage. The Union Army treated it harshly because it was the first state of the Southern Confederacy.", "This event is a representative example showing the brutality of war in American history. Like Korea''s Korean War, it is a tragic history of people from the same country fighting each other."], "sentences": [{"text": "1865년 미국 남북전쟁 당시 연방군(Union Army)이 사우스캐롤라이나주를 공격했어요.", "translation": "During the American Civil War in 1865, the Union Army attacked South Carolina.", "vocab": [{"ko": "남북전쟁", "en": "the (American) Civil War"}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time; during"}, {"ko": "연방군", "en": "Union Army; federal forces"}, {"ko": "공격하다", "en": "to attack"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 주는 미국에서 가장 먼저 연방에서 탈퇴한 곳이었어요.", "translation": "This state was the first in the United States to secede from the Union.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가장", "en": "most; the most"}, {"ko": "탈퇴하다", "en": "to withdraw; to secede"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 탈퇴하다 (to withdraw) → 탈퇴한 곳 (the place that withdrew).", "example_in_sentence": "탈퇴한 곳"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이었어요 (past of 이다)", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 (to be) after a consonant. 곳 → 곳이었어요 (was the place).", "example_in_sentence": "곳이었어요"}]}, {"text": "연방군은 사우스캐롤라이나가 남북전쟁을 시작했다고 생각했어요.", "translation": "The Union Army thought that South Carolina had started the Civil War.", "vocab": [{"ko": "시작하다", "en": "to start; to begin"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 생각하다", "exp": "Expression of indirect thought or opinion. The clause ~다고 marks reported/quoted speech, with 생각했어요 indicating past thinking.", "example_in_sentence": "남북전쟁을 시작했다고 생각했어요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 이 지역에 도착했을 때 큰 복수를 했어요.", "translation": "So when they arrived in this region, they took harsh revenge.", "vocab": [{"ko": "도착하다", "en": "to arrive"}, {"ko": "복수", "en": "revenge; retaliation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었을 때", "exp": "Means ''when (something) happened''. 도착하다 → 도착했을 때 (when they arrived).", "example_in_sentence": "도착했을 때"}]}, {"text": "특히 찰스턴 지역은 심각한 피해를 받았어요.", "translation": "Particularly, the Charleston region suffered severe damage.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; particularly"}, {"ko": "심각하다", "en": "to be serious; to be severe"}, {"ko": "피해", "en": "damage; harm"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "피해를 받다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to suffer damage/harm''. Object 피해 + direct object marker 를 + 받다 (to receive).", "example_in_sentence": "심각한 피해를 받았어요"}]}, {"text": "연방군은 남부 동맹의 첫 번째 주라는 이유로 가혹하게 대했어요.", "translation": "The Union Army treated it harshly because it was the first state of the Southern Confederacy.", "vocab": [{"ko": "남부 동맹", "en": "Southern Confederacy"}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason; cause"}, {"ko": "가혹하다", "en": "to be harsh; to be cruel"}, {"ko": "대하다", "en": "to treat; to deal with"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는 이유로", "exp": "Means ''on the grounds that it is ...''. 첫 번째 주 + 라는 이유로 (because it was the first state).", "example_in_sentence": "첫 번째 주라는 이유로"}]}, {"text": "이 사건은 미국 역사에서 전쟁의 잔혹함을 보여주는 대표적인 사례예요.", "translation": "This incident is a representative example showing the cruelty of war in American history.", "vocab": [{"ko": "잔혹함", "en": "cruelty; brutality"}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to demonstrate"}, {"ko": "대표적", "en": "representative; typical"}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "example; case; instance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a present action. 보여주다 (to show) → 보여주는 사례 (an example that shows).", "example_in_sentence": "보여주는 대표적인 사례"}]}, {"text": "한국의 6.25 전쟁처럼 같은 나라 사람들끼리 싸운 비극적인 역사예요.", "translation": "Like Korea''s 6.25 War, it is a tragic history of people from the same country fighting each other.", "vocab": [{"ko": "싸우다", "en": "to fight; to quarrel"}, {"ko": "비극적", "en": "tragic"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~끼리", "exp": "Means ''among themselves'' (within one group). 같은 나라 사람들끼리 싸운 = people of the same country fought each other.", "example_in_sentence": "같은 나라 사람들끼리"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "남북전쟁", "en": "the (American) Civil War", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time; during", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연방군", "en": "Union Army; federal forces", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공격하다", "en": "to attack", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가장", "en": "most; the most", "note": ""}, {"ko": "탈퇴하다", "en": "to withdraw; to secede", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시작하다", "en": "to start; to begin", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도착하다", "en": "to arrive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "복수", "en": "revenge; retaliation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; particularly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "심각하다", "en": "to be serious; to be severe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "피해", "en": "damage; harm", "note": ""}, {"ko": "남부 동맹", "en": "Southern Confederacy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason; cause", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가혹하다", "en": "to be harsh; to be cruel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대하다", "en": "to treat; to deal with", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잔혹함", "en": "cruelty; brutality", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to demonstrate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대표적", "en": "representative; typical", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "example; case; instance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "싸우다", "en": "to fight; to quarrel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비극적", "en": "tragic", "note": ""}, {"word": "동맹", "reading": "dongmaeng", "meaning": "alliance; confederate; ally", "context": "남부 동맹의 첫 번째 주라는"}, {"word": "비극", "reading": "bigeuk", "meaning": "tragedy", "context": "비극적인 역사예요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes a noun with a completed action. 탈퇴하다 (to withdraw) → 탈퇴한 곳 (the place that withdrew).", "ex_ko": "이 주는 미국에서 가장 먼저 연방에서 탈퇴한 곳이었어요.", "ex_en": "This state was the first in the United States to secede from the Union."}, {"name": "~이었어요 (past of 이다)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 (to be) after a consonant. 곳 → 곳이었어요 (was the place).", "ex_ko": "이 주는 미국에서 가장 먼저 연방에서 탈퇴한 곳이었어요.", "ex_en": "This state was the first in the United States to secede from the Union."}, {"name": "~다고 생각하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Expression of indirect thought or opinion. The clause ~다고 marks reported/quoted speech, with 생각했어요 indicating past thinking.", "ex_ko": "연방군은 사우스캐롤라이나가 남북전쟁을 시작했다고 생각했어요.", "ex_en": "The Union Army thought that South Carolina had started the Civil War."}, {"name": "~았/었을 때", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''when (something) happened''. 도착하다 → 도착했을 때 (when they arrived).", "ex_ko": "그래서 이 지역에 도착했을 때 큰 복수를 했어요.", "ex_en": "So when they arrived in this region, they took harsh revenge."}, {"name": "~(이)라는 이유로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''on the grounds that it is ...''. 첫 번째 주 + 라는 이유로 (because it was the first state).", "ex_ko": "연방군은 남부 동맹의 첫 번째 주라는 이유로 가혹하게 대했어요.", "ex_en": "The Union Army treated it harshly because it was the first state of the Southern Confederacy."}, {"name": "~는 (verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes a noun with a present action. 보여주다 (to show) → 보여주는 사례 (an example that shows).", "ex_ko": "이 사건은 미국 역사에서 전쟁의 잔혹함을 보여주는 대표적인 사례예요.", "ex_en": "This incident is a representative example showing the cruelty of war in American history."}, {"name": "~끼리", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''among themselves'' (within one group). 같은 나라 사람들끼리 싸운 = people of the same country fought each other.", "ex_ko": "한국의 6.25 전쟁처럼 같은 나라 사람들끼리 싸운 비극적인 역사예요.", "ex_en": "Like Korea''s 6.25 War, it is a tragic history of people from the same country fighting each other."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mopuo9z9qbaa' and md5(translation) = '4948e3ff3169aa528e64d1b0ad09d314';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "인도에 다시라트 만지라는 사람이 살았어요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "In India, there lived a person named Dashrath Manjhi.", "vocab": [{"ko": "인도", "en": "India", "note": "proper noun, country name"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live, to reside", "note": "common verb"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": "basic noun"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past polite form indicating a completed action in the past.", "example_in_sentence": "살았어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "사람들은 그를 ''산 사나이''라고 불렀어요.", "idx": 1, "translation": "People called him the ''Mountain Man.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "사람들", "en": "people (plural)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call, to name", "note": "common verb"}, {"ko": "산", "en": "mountain", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Marks the direct object of the verb.", "example_in_sentence": "그를 ''산 사나이''라고"}, {"pattern": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past polite form.", "example_in_sentence": "불렀어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그에게는 슬픈 이야기가 있어요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "There is a sad story about him.", "vocab": [{"ko": "슬프다", "en": "to be sad", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ (attributive modifier)", "exp": "Modifies a noun with an adjective or past verb.", "example_in_sentence": "슬픈 이야기"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그의 아내가 아팠을 때 일이에요.", "idx": 3, "translation": "It was when his wife was ill.", "vocab": [{"ko": "아내", "en": "wife", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아프다", "en": "to be sick, ill", "note": "common adjective"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/ㄹ 때", "exp": "Temporal clause marking ''when'' or ''at the time of.''", "example_in_sentence": "아팠을 때"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "집과 병원 사이에 큰 산이 있었어요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "There was a large mountain between his house and the hospital.", "vocab": [{"ko": "집", "en": "house, home", "note": ""}, {"ko": "병원", "en": "hospital", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사이", "en": "between, space", "note": ""}, {"ko": "크다", "en": "to be large, big", "note": "common adjective"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ (attributive modifier)", "exp": "Modifies a noun.", "example_in_sentence": "큰 산"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "산을 돌아가려면 시간이 너무 오래 걸렸어요.", "idx": 5, "translation": "Going around the mountain took far too long.", "vocab": [{"ko": "돌아가다", "en": "to go around, to detour", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time (duration)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to take (time), to require", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~으려면", "exp": "Conditional ''in order to'' or ''if one wants to.''", "example_in_sentence": "돌아가려면"}, {"pattern": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past polite form.", "example_in_sentence": "걸렸어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "결국 아내는 의사를 만나지 못하고 세상을 떠났어요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "In the end, his wife passed away without being able to see a doctor.", "vocab": [{"ko": "결국", "en": "in the end, eventually", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만나다", "en": "to meet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "세상을 떠나다", "en": "to pass away, to leave the world", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지 않고", "exp": "Negation with conjunctive form ''without doing'' or ''and not.''", "example_in_sentence": "만나지 못하고"}, {"pattern": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past polite form.", "example_in_sentence": "떠났어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "다시라트는 매우 슬펐어요.", "idx": 7, "translation": "Dashrath was very sad.", "vocab": [{"ko": "매우", "en": "very, greatly", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "슬프다", "en": "to be sad", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past polite form of copula/adjective.", "example_in_sentence": "슬펐어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그래서 놀라운 일을 시작했어요.", "idx": 8, "translation": "So he started doing something amazing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그래서", "en": "so, therefore", "note": "conjunction"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be amazing; to be surprising", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일", "en": "thing, work, deed", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ (attributive modifier)", "exp": "Modifies a noun.", "example_in_sentence": "놀라운 일"}, {"pattern": "~기 시작하다", "exp": "Begins to do; marks the start of an action.", "example_in_sentence": "시작했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "망치와 끌만 가지고 산을 깎기 시작했어요.", "idx": 9, "translation": "He began chiseling the mountain with only a hammer and chisel.", "vocab": [{"ko": "망치", "en": "hammer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "끌", "en": "chisel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깎다", "en": "to carve, to chisel, to cut", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~만 (exclusive particle)", "exp": "Marks ''only'' or ''nothing but.''", "example_in_sentence": "망치와 끌만"}, {"pattern": "~기 시작하다", "exp": "Began to do; marks the start of an action.", "example_in_sentence": "깎기 시작했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "다른 사람들이 같은 일을 겪지 않게 하려고 했어요.", "idx": 10, "translation": "He wanted to prevent other people from experiencing the same thing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다른", "en": "other, different", "note": ""}, {"ko": "겪다", "en": "to experience, to go through", "note": ""}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~게 하다", "exp": "Causative ''to make/cause someone to do.''", "example_in_sentence": "겪지 않게 하려고"}, {"pattern": "~으려고 하다", "exp": "Intention or purpose ''tried to'' or ''intended to.''", "example_in_sentence": "하려고 했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그는 22년 동안 매일 산을 깎았어요.", "idx": 11, "translation": "He chiseled the mountain every day for 22 years.", "vocab": [{"ko": "매일", "en": "every day, daily", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during, for (a period)", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "exp": "Progressive action; ongoing over time.", "example_in_sentence": "깎았어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "마침내 110미터 길이의 길을 만들었어요.", "idx": 12, "translation": "Finally, he created a road 110 meters long.", "vocab": [{"ko": "마침내", "en": "finally, at last", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "미터", "en": "meter (unit of length)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "길이", "en": "length, distance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "길", "en": "road, path", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ (attributive modifier)", "exp": "Modifies a noun.", "example_in_sentence": "110미터 길이의"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이제 마을 사람들은 빨리 병원에 갈 수 있게 되었어요.", "idx": 13, "translation": "Now the villagers can get to the hospital quickly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "마을", "en": "village", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빨리", "en": "quickly, fast", "note": "adverb"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Can, be able to; expresses possibility or capability.", "example_in_sentence": "갈 수 있게"}, {"pattern": "~아/어지다 (resultative)", "exp": "Became, turned; marks a change of state.", "example_in_sentence": "되었어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한 사람의 사랑이 만든 기적이에요.", "idx": 14, "translation": "It is a miracle created by one person''s love.", "vocab": [{"ko": "한", "en": "one, a single", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사랑", "en": "love", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기적", "en": "miracle", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ (attributive modifier)", "exp": "Modifies a noun.", "example_in_sentence": "만든 기적"}], "analysis": []}], "version": "p2"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "인도", "en": "India", "note": "proper noun, country name"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live, to reside", "note": "common verb"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": "basic noun"}, {"ko": "사람들", "en": "people (plural)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call, to name", "note": "common verb"}, {"ko": "산", "en": "mountain", "note": ""}, {"ko": "슬프다", "en": "to be sad", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아내", "en": "wife", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아프다", "en": "to be sick, ill", "note": "common adjective"}, {"ko": "집", "en": "house, home", "note": ""}, {"ko": "병원", "en": "hospital", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사이", "en": "between, space", "note": ""}, {"ko": "크다", "en": "to be large, big", "note": "common adjective"}, {"ko": "돌아가다", "en": "to go around, to detour", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time (duration)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to take (time), to require", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결국", "en": "in the end, eventually", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만나다", "en": "to meet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "세상을 떠나다", "en": "to pass away, to leave the world", "note": ""}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very, greatly", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "그래서", "en": "so, therefore", "note": "conjunction"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be amazing; to be surprising", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일", "en": "thing, work, deed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "망치", "en": "hammer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "끌", "en": "chisel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깎다", "en": "to carve, to chisel, to cut", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다른", "en": "other, different", "note": ""}, {"ko": "겪다", "en": "to experience, to go through", "note": ""}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same", "note": ""}, {"ko": "매일", "en": "every day, daily", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during, for (a period)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마침내", "en": "finally, at last", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "미터", "en": "meter (unit of length)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "길이", "en": "length, distance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "길", "en": "road, path", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마을", "en": "village", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빨리", "en": "quickly, fast", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "한", "en": "one, a single", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사랑", "en": "love", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기적", "en": "miracle", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mopuowemi129' and md5(translation) = '8c9b91da0cbfc9fd9434a4c1fea837f9';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["India is a country that produces 40-50% of the world''s mangoes. It grows over 20 million tons of mangoes every year.", "However, the mangoes that India exports account for less than 1% of its total production. According to some data, it exports only 0.12%.", "This is because Indian people really love mangoes. Most of the mangoes are consumed domestically.", "Korea also imports a lot of mangoes, but mainly from the Philippines or Thailand. It seems there aren''t many opportunities to taste Indian mangoes."], "sentences": [{"text": "인도는 전 세계 망고의 40~50%를 생산하는 나라예요.", "translation": "India is a country that produces 40~50% of mangoes worldwide.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전 세계", "en": "the whole world; worldwide"}, {"ko": "생산하다", "en": "to produce"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a present action. 생산하다 (to produce) → 생산하는 나라 (a country that produces).", "example_in_sentence": "생산하는 나라"}]}, {"text": "매년 2천만 톤이 넘는 망고를 키우고 있어요.", "translation": "Every year, India grows more than 20 million tons of mangoes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "매년", "en": "every year; annually"}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to go over"}, {"ko": "키우다", "en": "to grow; to raise"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker. Indicates ongoing action: 있다 (to exist) attached to verb stem with ~고.", "example_in_sentence": "키우고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 인도가 수출하는 망고는 전체 생산량의 1%도 안 돼요.", "translation": "However, the mangoes India exports account for less than 1% of total production.", "vocab": [{"ko": "수출하다", "en": "to export"}, {"ko": "생산량", "en": "production volume"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 안 되다", "exp": "Means ''not even (that amount)''. 1%도 안 돼요 (is not even 1%).", "example_in_sentence": "1%도 안 돼요"}]}, {"text": "어떤 자료에 따르면 0.12%밖에 수출하지 않는다고 해요.", "translation": "According to some data, India exports only 0.12% of them.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자료", "en": "data; material; information"}, {"ko": "따르다", "en": "to follow; to go by"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에 따르면", "exp": "Combines location particle ''~에'' with verb ''따르다'' in conditional form. Means ''according to'' or ''based on''.", "example_in_sentence": "어떤 자료에 따르면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~밖에 ~지 않다", "exp": "밖에 with a negative verb means ''only''. 0.12%밖에 수출하지 않는다 (exports only 0.12%).", "example_in_sentence": "0.12%밖에 수출하지 않는다고"}]}, {"text": "이는 인도 사람들이 망고를 정말 좋아하기 때문이에요.", "translation": "This is because Indian people really like mangoes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정말", "en": "really; very much"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~기 때문이에요", "exp": "Nominalizer ''~기'' + noun ''때문'' (reason/cause) with copula. Expresses causation: ''because of the fact that''.", "example_in_sentence": "좋아하기 때문이에요"}]}, {"text": "대부분의 망고를 국내에서 소비하고 있어요.", "translation": "Most of the mangoes are consumed within the country.", "vocab": [{"ko": "대부분", "en": "majority; most; the greater part"}, {"ko": "소비하다", "en": "to consume"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect. Shows ongoing consumption happening currently.", "example_in_sentence": "소비하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "한국도 망고를 많이 수입하지만 주로 필리핀이나 태국에서 가져와요.", "translation": "Korea also imports many mangoes, but mainly brings them from the Philippines or Thailand.", "vocab": [{"ko": "수입하다", "en": "to import"}, {"ko": "주로", "en": "mainly; primarily; chiefly"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만", "exp": "Conjunctive ending connecting two contrasting clauses. First clause affirms an action; second introduces a limitation.", "example_in_sentence": "수입하지만"}]}, {"text": "인도 망고를 맛볼 기회는 많지 않은 것 같아요.", "translation": "It seems there are not many opportunities to taste Indian mangoes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "맛보다", "en": "to taste; to try"}, {"ko": "기회", "en": "chance; opportunity"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것 같다", "exp": "Means ''it seems that ...'' after an adjective. 많지 않다 → 많지 않은 것 같아요 (there don''t seem to be many).", "example_in_sentence": "많지 않은 것 같아요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "전 세계", "en": "the whole world; worldwide", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생산하다", "en": "to produce", "note": ""}, {"ko": "매년", "en": "every year; annually", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to go over", "note": ""}, {"ko": "키우다", "en": "to grow; to raise", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수출하다", "en": "to export", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생산량", "en": "production volume", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자료", "en": "data; material; information", "note": ""}, {"ko": "따르다", "en": "to follow; to go by", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really; very much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대부분", "en": "majority; most; the greater part", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소비하다", "en": "to consume", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수입하다", "en": "to import", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주로", "en": "mainly; primarily; chiefly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "맛보다", "en": "to taste; to try", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기회", "en": "chance; opportunity", "note": ""}, {"word": "국내", "reading": "gung-nae", "meaning": "domestic / within the country", "context": "대부분의 망고를 국내에서 소비하고 있어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~는 (verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes a noun with a present action. 생산하다 (to produce) → 생산하는 나라 (a country that produces).", "ex_ko": "인도는 전 세계 망고의 40~50%를 생산하는 나라예요.", "ex_en": "India is a country that produces 40~50% of mangoes worldwide."}, {"name": "~고 있어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker. Indicates ongoing action: 있다 (to exist) attached to verb stem with ~고.", "ex_ko": "매년 2천만 톤이 넘는 망고를 키우고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Every year, India grows more than 20 million tons of mangoes."}, {"name": "~도 안 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''not even (that amount)''. 1%도 안 돼요 (is not even 1%).", "ex_ko": "하지만 인도가 수출하는 망고는 전체 생산량의 1%도 안 돼요.", "ex_en": "However, the mangoes India exports account for less than 1% of total production."}, {"name": "~밖에 ~지 않다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "밖에 with a negative verb means ''only''. 0.12%밖에 수출하지 않는다 (exports only 0.12%).", "ex_ko": "어떤 자료에 따르면 0.12%밖에 수출하지 않는다고 해요.", "ex_en": "According to some data, India exports only 0.12% of them."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Conjunctive ending connecting two contrasting clauses. First clause affirms an action; second introduces a limitation.", "ex_ko": "한국도 망고를 많이 수입하지만 주로 필리핀이나 태국에서 가져와요.", "ex_en": "Korea also imports many mangoes, but mainly brings them from the Philippines or Thailand."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 것 같다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''it seems that ...'' after an adjective. 많지 않다 → 많지 않은 것 같아요 (there don''t seem to be many).", "ex_ko": "인도 망고를 맛볼 기회는 많지 않은 것 같아요.", "ex_en": "It seems there are not many opportunities to taste Indian mangoes."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mopupfjm9b30' and md5(translation) = '8bbfd7a2e835be58fadea8cf7f27b6f1';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A Japanese magazine contains something special. It''s a real marriage registration form. Inside the magazine sold at bookstores, there is an official document recognized by the government.", "If you fill out this document, you can actually get married. You buy the magazine, write the necessary information, and submit it to the government office. In Japan, this method is possible.", "In Korea, you have to go to the district office or community service center to register your marriage. You cannot obtain marriage documents from a magazine. Different countries have different methods for marriage registration.", "Many people find this news interesting. It''s really fascinating that one magazine can change your life."], "sentences": [{"text": "일본의 한 잡지에 특별한 것이 들어있어요.", "translation": "A Japanese magazine contains something special.", "vocab": [{"ko": "잡지", "en": "magazine", "note": "noun for periodical publications"}, {"ko": "들어있다", "en": "to be contained in", "note": "passive form of 들어가다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ/은 것", "exp": "nominalizes a preceding clause to refer to ''a thing'' or ''something''", "example_in_sentence": "특별한 것"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "바로 진짜 결혼 신청서예요.", "translation": "It''s a real marriage registration form.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바로", "en": "precisely, exactly", "note": "adverb emphasizing the exact identity of something"}, {"ko": "신청서", "en": "application form", "note": "noun: 신청 (application) + 서 (document)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㅂ니다 / ~예요", "exp": "simple present copula statement expressing what something is", "example_in_sentence": "신청서예요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "서점에서 파는 잡지 안에 정부에서 인정하는 공식 서류가 있어요.", "translation": "Inside a magazine sold at bookstores, there is an official document recognized by the government.", "vocab": [{"ko": "서점", "en": "bookstore", "note": "noun: 서 (book) + 점 (store)"}, {"ko": "인정하다", "en": "to recognize, acknowledge", "note": "verb used for official acceptance"}, {"ko": "공식", "en": "official", "note": "adjective/noun for formal or official status"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 / ~ㄴ (relative clause)", "exp": "modifies the following noun with descriptive information", "example_in_sentence": "서점에서 파는 잡지, 정부에서 인정하는 공식 서류"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 서류를 작성하면 실제로 결혼할 수 있어요.", "translation": "If you fill out this document, you can actually get married.", "vocab": [{"ko": "작성하다", "en": "to fill out, compose", "note": "formal verb for writing or completing documents"}, {"ko": "실제로", "en": "actually, in reality", "note": "adverb emphasizing true or actual occurrence"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~면 ~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "conditional statement expressing possibility: ''if X happens, you can do Y''", "example_in_sentence": "작성하면 실제로 결혼할 수 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "잡지를 사서 필요한 내용을 쓰고 관청에 내면 돼요.", "translation": "You just buy the magazine, fill in the necessary details, and submit it to a government office.", "vocab": [{"ko": "관청", "en": "government office", "note": "formal noun for administrative offices"}, {"ko": "내다", "en": "to submit, turn in", "note": "verb for handing over documents officially"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 ~면 되다", "exp": "sequence of actions connected by ~고 with conditional ~면 되다 (it will work/suffice)", "example_in_sentence": "사서 필요한 내용을 쓰고 관청에 내면 돼요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "일본에서는 이런 방법도 가능해요.", "translation": "In Japan, this kind of method is also possible.", "vocab": [{"ko": "방법", "en": "method, way", "note": "noun for procedures or means"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~도", "exp": "particle meaning ''also'' or ''even'', indicating inclusion of an additional example", "example_in_sentence": "이런 방법도 가능해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한국에서는 구청이나 동사무소에 가야 결혼 신고를 할 수 있어요.", "translation": "In Korea, you have to go to a district office or community service office to register your marriage.", "vocab": [{"ko": "구청", "en": "district office", "note": "local government office (구 + 청)"}, {"ko": "동사무소", "en": "community service office", "note": "local administrative office (neighborhood level)"}, {"ko": "신고", "en": "registration, report", "note": "noun for official notification or registration"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~아/어야 ~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "expresses necessity: ''must do X in order to do Y'' or ''can only do Y by doing X''", "example_in_sentence": "가야 결혼 신고를 할 수 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "잡지에서 결혼 서류를 구할 수는 없어요.", "translation": "You cannot obtain marriage documents from a magazine in Korea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "구하다", "en": "to obtain, get", "note": "verb for acquiring or finding something"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 수 없다", "exp": "negative possibility: ''cannot do'' or ''it is impossible to do''", "example_in_sentence": "구할 수 없어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "나라마다 결혼 신고 방법이 다르네요.", "translation": "The marriage registration method differs from country to country.", "vocab": [{"ko": "나라", "en": "country", "note": "noun + ~마다 (distributive particle meaning ''per'' or ''each'')"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~네요", "exp": "ending expressing realization or discovery of something new; ''I see that...''", "example_in_sentence": "다르네요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이 소식을 신기하게 생각해요.", "translation": "Many people find this news fascinating.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소식", "en": "news, information", "note": "noun for news or tidings"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be interesting, surprising, novel", "note": "adjective expressing something seems new or remarkable"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~게 생각하다", "exp": "verb phrase meaning ''to think of something in a certain way'' or ''to regard as''", "example_in_sentence": "신기하게 생각해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "잡지 한 권으로 인생이 바뀔 수 있다니 정말 흥미로워요.", "translation": "The fact that one''s life can change with just one magazine is truly fascinating.", "vocab": [{"ko": "인생", "en": "life, one''s life", "note": "noun combining 인 (person) + 생 (life)"}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change", "note": "passive/intransitive verb for undergoing change"}, {"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting, fascinating", "note": "adjective expressing something is interesting or engaging"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 수 있다 + ~ㄴ/다니", "exp": "''~ㄴ/다니'' expresses surprise or admiration about something; literally ''that it can change is surprising''", "example_in_sentence": "바뀔 수 있다니 정말 흥미로워요"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "잡지", "en": "magazine", "note": "noun for periodical publications"}, {"ko": "들어있다", "en": "to be contained in", "note": "passive form of 들어가다"}, {"ko": "바로", "en": "precisely, exactly", "note": "adverb emphasizing the exact identity of something"}, {"ko": "신청서", "en": "application form", "note": "noun: 신청 (application) + 서 (document)"}, {"ko": "서점", "en": "bookstore", "note": "noun: 서 (book) + 점 (store)"}, {"ko": "인정하다", "en": "to recognize, acknowledge", "note": "verb used for official acceptance"}, {"ko": "공식", "en": "official", "note": "adjective/noun for formal or official status"}, {"ko": "작성하다", "en": "to fill out, compose", "note": "formal verb for writing or completing documents"}, {"ko": "실제로", "en": "actually, in reality", "note": "adverb emphasizing true or actual occurrence"}, {"ko": "관청", "en": "government office", "note": "formal noun for administrative offices"}, {"ko": "내다", "en": "to submit, turn in", "note": "verb for handing over documents officially"}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method, way", "note": "noun for procedures or means"}, {"ko": "구청", "en": "district office", "note": "local government office (구 + 청)"}, {"ko": "동사무소", "en": "community service office", "note": "local administrative office (neighborhood level)"}, {"ko": "신고", "en": "registration, report", "note": "noun for official notification or registration"}, {"ko": "구하다", "en": "to obtain, get", "note": "verb for acquiring or finding something"}, {"ko": "나라", "en": "country", "note": "noun + ~마다 (distributive particle meaning ''per'' or ''each'')"}, {"ko": "소식", "en": "news, information", "note": "noun for news or tidings"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be interesting, surprising, novel", "note": "adjective expressing something seems new or remarkable"}, {"ko": "인생", "en": "life, one''s life", "note": "noun combining 인 (person) + 생 (life)"}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change", "note": "passive/intransitive verb for undergoing change"}, {"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting, fascinating", "note": "adjective expressing something is interesting or engaging"}, {"word": "결혼 신청서", "reading": "gyolhon sincheongseo", "meaning": "marriage application form / marriage proposal document", "context": "바로 진짜 결혼 신청서예요"}, {"word": "정부", "reading": "jeongbu", "meaning": "government", "context": "정부에서 인정하는 공식 서류가 있어요"}, {"word": "서류", "reading": "seoryu", "meaning": "document / paperwork", "context": "정부에서 인정하는 공식 서류가 있어요"}, {"word": "결혼 신고", "reading": "gyolhon singgo", "meaning": "marriage registration / marriage notification", "context": "결혼 신고를 할 수 있어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mopupzvwbp09' and md5(translation) = 'c0b0c396cd1aacfa7b0044129c41bd64';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In China, you can order food delivery while riding a high-speed train. When the train arrives at the next station, the food you ordered is delivered right to your seat. This service is very convenient for passengers. You can easily receive delicious food during a long journey. You can order simply through a smartphone app. I wish Korean high-speed trains like KTX (Korea Train eXpress) or SRT (Super Rapid Train) had this kind of service too. It seems like you could order local specialties while traveling from Seoul to Busan. China''s delivery service is a good example of technological advancement. It seems like more countries will adopt similar services in the future.", "Korea''s teacher shortage becomes serious, causing disruption to school classes", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A popular trend", "The US and China resume talks over trade issues", "\"Talking pig\" becomes a social media star", "The \"nothing maxing\" trend of doing nothing spreads"], "sentences": [{"text": "중국에서는 고속열차를 타면서 음식 배달을 주문할 수 있어요.", "translation": "In China, you can order food delivery while riding a high-speed train.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고속열차", "en": "high-speed train"}, {"ko": "음식 배달", "en": "food delivery"}, {"ko": "주문하다", "en": "to order"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서", "exp": "Connects two actions happening at the same time (''while''). 타다 → 타면서 = while riding.", "example_in_sentence": "타면서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Modal expressing possibility or ability. ~ㄹ 수 있어요 = can/is able to, in polite present form.", "example_in_sentence": "주문할 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "열차가 다음 역에 도착하면 주문한 음식이 바로 좌석까지 배달돼요.", "translation": "When the train arrives at the next station, the ordered food is delivered right to the seat.", "vocab": [{"ko": "역", "en": "station"}, {"ko": "도착하다", "en": "to arrive"}, {"ko": "좌석", "en": "seat"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "Conditional ending meaning ''if/when''. 도착하다 → 도착하면 = when it arrives.", "example_in_sentence": "도착하면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past participle modifier)", "exp": "Past participle modifying the noun that follows. ~한 음식 = the ordered/that-was-ordered food.", "example_in_sentence": "주문한 음식"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지", "exp": "Particle indicating extent or limit. Shows that delivery reaches all the way to the seat.", "example_in_sentence": "좌석까지"}]}, {"text": "이 서비스는 승객들에게 매우 편리한 서비스예요.", "translation": "This is a very convenient service for passengers.", "vocab": [{"ko": "승객", "en": "passenger"}, {"ko": "편리하다", "en": "to be convenient"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "Particle indicating the indirect object or recipient. Shows to/for whom the service is convenient.", "example_in_sentence": "승객들에게"}]}, {"text": "긴 여행 중에 맛있는 음식을 쉽게 받을 수 있거든요.", "translation": "Because you can easily receive delicious food during a long trip.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여행", "en": "trip; journey"}, {"ko": "맛있다", "en": "to be delicious"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 중에", "exp": "Temporal expression indicating during/in the middle of a period or action.", "example_in_sentence": "여행 중에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~거든요", "exp": "Causal/explanatory ending in polite form. Explains the reason why the previous statement is true.", "example_in_sentence": "받을 수 있거든요"}]}, {"text": "스마트폰 앱을 통해서 간단하게 주문할 수 있어요.", "translation": "You can order simply through a smartphone app.", "vocab": [{"ko": "앱", "en": "app"}, {"ko": "통하다", "en": "to go through; (통해서) through, via"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Modal expressing possibility or ability in polite present form.", "example_in_sentence": "주문할 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "한국의 케이티엑스(KTX)나 에스알티(SRT) 같은 고속열차에서도 이런 서비스가 있으면 좋겠어요.", "translation": "I wish that high-speed trains like KTX or SRT in Korea would also have such a service.", "vocab": [{"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same; like"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~(이)나", "exp": "Particle meaning ''or'' between nouns. KTX나 SRT = KTX or SRT.", "example_in_sentence": "케이티엑스(KTX)나 에스알티(SRT)"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 좋겠다", "exp": "Conditional expression of wish or desire. ~면 좋겠어요 = I wish/hope that... would happen.", "example_in_sentence": "있으면 좋겠어요"}]}, {"text": "서울에서 부산까지 가는 동안 지역 특산품도 주문할 수 있을 것 같아요.", "translation": "It seems like you could also order local specialties while going from Seoul to Busan.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특산품", "en": "local specialty; specialty product"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 동안", "exp": "Temporal expression indicating during a period or span of time/distance.", "example_in_sentence": "가는 동안"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 것 같다", "exp": "Expresses a guess: ''it seems like ~ will/could''. 있다 → 있을 것 같아요 = it seems you could.", "example_in_sentence": "주문할 수 있을 것 같아요"}]}, {"text": "중국의 이런 배달 서비스는 기술 발전을 잘 보여주는 예예요.", "translation": "Such a delivery service in China is an example that well demonstrates technological development.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기술", "en": "technology; technique"}, {"ko": "발전", "en": "development; progress"}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to demonstrate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present modifier)", "exp": "Present-tense modifier for verbs. 보여주다 → 보여주는 예 = an example that shows.", "example_in_sentence": "보여주는 예"}]}, {"text": "앞으로 더 많은 나라에서 비슷한 서비스를 도입할 것 같아요.", "translation": "It seems like more countries will introduce similar services in the future.", "vocab": [{"ko": "앞으로", "en": "in the future; going forward"}, {"ko": "도입하다", "en": "to introduce; to adopt"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/ㄹ 것 같다", "exp": "Modal expression indicating conjecture or prediction about the future. ~ㄹ 것 같아요 = it seems like... will happen.", "example_in_sentence": "도입할 것 같아요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "고속열차", "en": "high-speed train", "note": ""}, {"ko": "음식 배달", "en": "food delivery", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주문하다", "en": "to order", "note": ""}, {"ko": "역", "en": "station", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도착하다", "en": "to arrive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "좌석", "en": "seat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "승객", "en": "passenger", "note": ""}, {"ko": "편리하다", "en": "to be convenient", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여행", "en": "trip; journey", "note": ""}, {"ko": "맛있다", "en": "to be delicious", "note": ""}, {"ko": "앱", "en": "app", "note": ""}, {"ko": "통하다", "en": "to go through; (통해서) through, via", "note": ""}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same; like", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특산품", "en": "local specialty; specialty product", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technology; technique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발전", "en": "development; progress", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to demonstrate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "앞으로", "en": "in the future; going forward", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도입하다", "en": "to introduce; to adopt", "note": ""}, {"word": "배달", "reading": "baedal", "meaning": "delivery (of goods, food, etc.)", "context": "고속열차를 타면서 음식 배달을 주문할"}, {"word": "기술 발전", "reading": "gisul baljeon", "meaning": "technological advancement; technological progress", "context": "이런 배달 서비스는 기술 발전을 잘"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connects two actions happening at the same time (''while''). 타다 → 타면서 = while riding.", "ex_ko": "중국에서는 고속열차를 타면서 음식 배달을 주문할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "In China, you can order food delivery while riding a high-speed train."}, {"name": "~을/ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Modal expressing possibility or ability. ~ㄹ 수 있어요 = can/is able to, in polite present form.", "ex_ko": "중국에서는 고속열차를 타면서 음식 배달을 주문할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "In China, you can order food delivery while riding a high-speed train."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past participle modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past participle modifying the noun that follows. ~한 음식 = the ordered/that-was-ordered food.", "ex_ko": "열차가 다음 역에 도착하면 주문한 음식이 바로 좌석